window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1"]={"id":"CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1","title":"CGL 23 OCT 2026 SHIFT 1","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000071681","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Completing","question":{"en":"Select an appropriate figure from the four options that would complete the figure.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"चार विकल्पों में से वह उपयुक्त आकृति चुनिए जो दी गई आकृति को पूर्ण करेगी।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In every successive box the arrow reverses its direction and the square moves to the diagonally opposite corner, that is, the square and the semicircle beside it exchange their places.<br>In the fourth box the arrow points to the left with the square at the bottom-right corner; therefore in the fifth box the arrow must point to the right and the square must be at the bottom-left corner, with one semicircle at the top and the other at the bottom.<br>Only option (3) shows exactly this arrangement.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3).</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अगले बक्से में तीर अपनी दिशा उलट देता है तथा वर्ग विकर्णतः विपरीत कोने में चला जाता है, अर्थात् वर्ग और उसके पास वाला अर्धवृत्त अपने स्थान बदल लेते हैं।<br>चौथे बक्से में तीर बाईं ओर है और वर्ग नीचे-दाएँ कोने में है, इसलिए पाँचवें बक्से में तीर दाईं ओर होना चाहिए तथा वर्ग नीचे-बाएँ कोने में, जबकि एक अर्धवृत्त ऊपर और दूसरा नीचे रहेगा।<br>यही व्यवस्था केवल विकल्प (3) में दिखाई गई है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q1.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q1_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q1_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q1_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q1_opt4.jpg"]}}},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000071682","section":"REASONING","topic":"Clock & Calendar","question":{"en":"What will be the angle formed between the hour hand and minute hand of a clock at 1:24 pm, when taken in a clockwise direction from the hour hand? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"जब घड़ी में 1:24 pm का समय है, तो घंटे की सुई से दक्षिणावर्त दिशा में मापने पर घंटे की सुई तथा मिनट की सुई के बीच कितना कोण बनेगा? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"180°"},"2":{"en":"82°"},"3":{"en":"102°"},"4":{"en":"95°"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Angle of the hour hand from 12 at 1:24 = 30 × 1 + 24 × 0.5 = 30 + 12 = 42°.<br>Angle of the minute hand from 12 = 24 × 6 = 144°.<br>Angle measured in the clockwise direction from the hour hand to the minute hand = 144° − 42° = 102°.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 102°.</b>","hi":"1:24 पर 12 से घंटे की सुई का कोण = 30 × 1 + 24 × 0.5 = 30 + 12 = 42°<br>12 से मिनट की सुई का कोण = 24 × 6 = 144°<br>घंटे की सुई से मिनट की सुई तक दक्षिणावर्त दिशा में कोण = 144° − 42° = 102°<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 102° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000071683","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"Identify the mirror image of the following figure when the mirror is placed to the right of the figure.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q3.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"जब दर्पण आकृति के दाईं ओर रखा जाए, तो दी गई आकृति का दर्पण प्रतिबिंब पहचानिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q3.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"When the mirror is on the right side, left and right of the figure get interchanged while the top and the bottom remain unchanged.<br>So the letters and symbols are read from the opposite end — G, B, L, %, N, @, R, E, K — and each of them is laterally inverted, while the two overlapping rectangles also swap their left-right positions.<br>Only option (3) shows all the letters and symbols correctly inverted and in the right order.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3).</b>","hi":"जब दर्पण दाईं ओर होता है तो आकृति के बाएँ और दाएँ भाग परस्पर बदल जाते हैं, जबकि ऊपर और नीचे के भाग वैसे ही रहते हैं।<br>अतः अक्षरों तथा चिह्नों का क्रम उलट जाता है — G, B, L, %, N, @, R, E, K — और प्रत्येक अक्षर पार्श्वतः उलटा हो जाता है; साथ ही दोनों अतिव्यापी आयत भी अपने बाएँ-दाएँ स्थान बदल लेते हैं।<br>केवल विकल्प (3) में सभी अक्षर तथा चिह्न सही क्रम में और सही ढंग से उलटे हुए हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q3.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q3_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q3_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q3_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q3_opt4.jpg"]}}},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000071684","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"In a group of 90 students, 40 take French, 30 take German, and 10 take both. How many students take only one language? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"90 विद्यार्थियों के एक समूह में 40 विद्यार्थी फ्रेंच लेते हैं, 30 जर्मन लेते हैं और 10 दोनों लेते हैं। कितने विद्यार्थी केवल एक भाषा लेते हैं? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"50"},"2":{"en":"40"},"3":{"en":"35"},"4":{"en":"30"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Students taking only French = 40 − 10 = 30.<br>Students taking only German = 30 − 10 = 20.<br>Students taking exactly one language = 30 + 20 = 50.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 50.</b>","hi":"केवल फ्रेंच लेने वाले विद्यार्थी = 40 − 10 = 30<br>केवल जर्मन लेने वाले विद्यार्थी = 30 − 10 = 20<br>ठीक एक भाषा लेने वाले विद्यार्थी = 30 + 20 = 50<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 50 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000071685","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"In a group of students, 18 play Cricket, 24 play Basketball, and 15 play Volleyball. 9 play both Cricket and Basketball, 7 play both Cricket and Volleyball, and 6 play both Basketball and Volleyball. 3 students play all three. How many play both Cricket and Basketball but not Volleyball? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"विद्यार्थियों के एक समूह में 18 क्रिकेट खेलते हैं, 24 बास्केटबॉल खेलते हैं और 15 वॉलीबॉल खेलते हैं। 9 क्रिकेट तथा बास्केटबॉल दोनों खेलते हैं, 7 क्रिकेट तथा वॉलीबॉल दोनों खेलते हैं और 6 बास्केटबॉल तथा वॉलीबॉल दोनों खेलते हैं। 3 विद्यार्थी तीनों खेल खेलते हैं। कितने विद्यार्थी क्रिकेट तथा बास्केटबॉल दोनों खेलते हैं, परंतु वॉलीबॉल नहीं खेलते? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6"},"2":{"en":"9"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"12"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The students playing all three games lie in the region common to Cricket, Basketball and Volleyball, and their number is 3.<br>Students playing both Cricket and Basketball but not Volleyball = 9 − 3 = 6.<br>The data about Volleyball only affects the other regions and does not change this value.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 6.</b>","hi":"तीनों खेल खेलने वाले विद्यार्थी क्रिकेट, बास्केटबॉल तथा वॉलीबॉल के उभयनिष्ठ भाग में आते हैं और उनकी संख्या 3 है।<br>क्रिकेट तथा बास्केटबॉल दोनों खेलने वाले, परंतु वॉलीबॉल न खेलने वाले विद्यार्थी = 9 − 3 = 6<br>वॉलीबॉल से संबंधित आँकड़े केवल अन्य भागों को प्रभावित करते हैं, इस मान को नहीं बदलते।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 6 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000071686","section":"REASONING","topic":"Embedded Figures","question":{"en":"Select the option figure in which the given figure is embedded (rotation is not allowed).<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q6.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस विकल्प आकृति का चयन कीजिए जिसमें दी गई आकृति अंतर्निहित है (घूर्णन की अनुमति नहीं है)।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q6.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The given figure is a zig-zag made of three slanted lines (up, down, up) of equal length.<br>Only option (4) contains exactly this zig-zag, unrotated, within its design — its left portion is built from the same sequence of slanted lines.<br>In options (1), (2) and (3) the diagonals are either differently inclined or do not form the required three-line zig-zag.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4).</b>","hi":"दी गई आकृति तीन समान लंबाई की तिर्यक रेखाओं (ऊपर, नीचे, ऊपर) से बनी एक ज़िग-ज़ैग है।<br>केवल विकल्प (4) में यही ज़िग-ज़ैग बिना घुमाए अपने डिज़ाइन में विद्यमान है — उसका बायाँ भाग इन्हीं तिर्यक रेखाओं के क्रम से बना है।<br>विकल्प (1), (2) तथा (3) में विकर्ण भिन्न झुकाव के हैं या अभीष्ट तीन-रेखा ज़िग-ज़ैग नहीं बनाते।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q6.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q6_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q6_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q6_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q6_opt4.jpg"]}}},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000071687","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"What will be the value of <b>m<sup>3</sup> + n<sup>3</sup> + p<sup>3</sup></b>, if <b>m + n + p = 0</b>? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि <b>m + n + p = 0</b> है, तो <b>m<sup>3</sup> + n<sup>3</sup> + p<sup>3</sup></b> का मान क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2mnp"},"2":{"en":"3mnp"},"3":{"en":"mnp(mn + np + mp)"},"4":{"en":"mnp"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"We use the identity:<br>m<sup>3</sup> + n<sup>3</sup> + p<sup>3</sup> − 3mnp = (m + n + p)(m<sup>2</sup> + n<sup>2</sup> + p<sup>2</sup> − mn − np − pm)<br>Since m + n + p = 0, the right-hand side becomes 0.<br>So m<sup>3</sup> + n<sup>3</sup> + p<sup>3</sup> − 3mnp = 0, i.e. m<sup>3</sup> + n<sup>3</sup> + p<sup>3</sup> = 3mnp.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 3mnp.</b>","hi":"हम सर्वसमिका का प्रयोग करते हैं:<br>m<sup>3</sup> + n<sup>3</sup> + p<sup>3</sup> − 3mnp = (m + n + p)(m<sup>2</sup> + n<sup>2</sup> + p<sup>2</sup> − mn − np − pm)<br>चूँकि m + n + p = 0 है, दायाँ पक्ष 0 हो जाता है।<br>अतः m<sup>3</sup> + n<sup>3</sup> + p<sup>3</sup> − 3mnp = 0, अर्थात् m<sup>3</sup> + n<sup>3</sup> + p<sup>3</sup> = 3mnp<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 3mnp है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000071688","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"A university noticed that students participating in international exchange programs achieved higher research output than other students. The university concluded that exchange programs directly improve academic productivity.<br><br>Which of the following, if true, would most weaken the university's conclusion? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक विश्वविद्यालय ने देखा कि अंतर्राष्ट्रीय छात्र-विनिमय कार्यक्रमों में भाग लेने वाले विद्यार्थियों का शोध-उत्पादन अन्य विद्यार्थियों की तुलना में अधिक रहा। विश्वविद्यालय ने यह निष्कर्ष निकाला कि विनिमय कार्यक्रम सीधे ही अकादमिक उत्पादकता बढ़ाते हैं।<br><br>निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा तथ्य, यदि सत्य हो, तो विश्वविद्यालय के निष्कर्ष को सबसे अधिक कमजोर करेगा? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Exchange students spent more time in laboratory activities.","hi":"विनिमय विद्यार्थियों ने प्रयोगशाला गतिविधियों में अधिक समय व्यतीत किया।"},"2":{"en":"Most exchange participants were selected from top-ranked students.","hi":"अधिकांश विनिमय प्रतिभागी शीर्ष श्रेणी के विद्यार्थियों में से चुने गए थे।"},"3":{"en":"International universities offered access to modern libraries.","hi":"अंतर्राष्ट्रीय विश्वविद्यालयों ने आधुनिक पुस्तकालयों तक पहुँच उपलब्ध कराई।"},"4":{"en":"Research publications increased across multiple disciplines.","hi":"अनेक विषयों में शोध-प्रकाशन बढ़े।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The conclusion treats the exchange programme as the cause of the higher research output.<br>If most exchange participants were already top-ranked students, then their superior output is explained by their own ability and motivation rather than by the programme — the selection itself, and not the exchange, produced the difference.<br>Options (1) and (3) give additional reasons that could only strengthen the causal link, and option (4) merely reports that publications rose in many disciplines, which does not weaken the conclusion.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Most exchange participants were selected from top-ranked students.</b>","hi":"निष्कर्ष में विनिमय कार्यक्रम को अधिक शोध-उत्पादन का कारण मान लिया गया है।<br>यदि अधिकांश विनिमय प्रतिभागी पहले से ही शीर्ष श्रेणी के विद्यार्थी थे, तो उनका बेहतर उत्पादन उनकी अपनी योग्यता तथा लगन से समझाया जा सकता है, कार्यक्रम से नहीं — अंतर का कारण स्वयं चयन है, विनिमय नहीं।<br>विकल्प (1) तथा (3) कारण-संबंध को और मजबूत ही करते हैं, और विकल्प (4) केवल यह बताता है कि अनेक विषयों में प्रकाशन बढ़े, जिससे निष्कर्ष कमजोर नहीं होता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): अधिकांश विनिमय प्रतिभागी शीर्ष श्रेणी के विद्यार्थियों में से चुने गए थे।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000071689","section":"REASONING","topic":"Order & Ranking","question":{"en":"In a row of boys, Arjun is 9th from the left, and Ravi is 15th from the right. If they interchange their positions, Arjun becomes 20th from the left. How many boys are there in the row? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"लड़कों की एक पंक्ति में अर्जुन बाएँ से 9वें स्थान पर है और रवि दाएँ से 15वें स्थान पर है। यदि वे अपने-अपने स्थान बदल लें, तो अर्जुन बाएँ से 20वें स्थान पर आ जाता है। पंक्ति में कितने लड़के हैं? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"31"},"2":{"en":"32"},"3":{"en":"33"},"4":{"en":"34"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"After the interchange Arjun occupies Ravi's original seat, and that seat is 20th from the left. So Ravi's position is 20th from the left and 15th from the right.<br>Total number of boys = 20 + 15 − 1 = 34.<br>(Arjun's original 9th place is not needed once the two positions are added.)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 34.</b>","hi":"स्थान बदलने के बाद अर्जुन रवि के मूल स्थान पर आ जाता है, और वह स्थान बाएँ से 20वाँ है। अतः रवि का स्थान बाएँ से 20वाँ तथा दाएँ से 15वाँ है।<br>लड़कों की कुल संख्या = 20 + 15 − 1 = 34<br>(दोनों स्थान जोड़ लेने पर अर्जुन के मूल 9वें स्थान की आवश्यकता नहीं रहती।)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 34 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000071690","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Complete the following series.<br><b>5, 1, 35, 4, 315, 9, 3465, 16, ?</b> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित श्रेणी को पूरा कीजिए।<br><b>5, 1, 35, 4, 315, 9, 3465, 16, ?</b> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25689"},"2":{"en":"36809"},"3":{"en":"45045"},"4":{"en":"43680"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The series is formed by two interleaved series.<br>Even places: 1, 4, 9, 16 — the squares of 1, 2, 3, 4.<br>Odd places: 5, 35, 315, 3465, ? — each term is multiplied by successive odd numbers:<br>5 × 7 = 35, 35 × 9 = 315, 315 × 11 = 3465, 3465 × 13 = 45045.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 45045.</b>","hi":"श्रेणी दो अंतर्गुम्फित श्रेणियों से बनी है।<br>सम स्थान: 1, 4, 9, 16 — 1, 2, 3, 4 के वर्ग।<br>विषम स्थान: 5, 35, 315, 3465, ? — प्रत्येक पद क्रमागत विषम संख्याओं से गुणा होता है:<br>5 × 7 = 35, 35 × 9 = 315, 315 × 11 = 3465, 3465 × 13 = 45045<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 45045 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000071691","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Completing","question":{"en":"Complete the pattern in fig. (X) by selecting one of the figures from the four alternatives:<br>Figure (X):<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q11.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"आकृति (X) में दिए गए पैटर्न को चार विकल्पों में से एक आकृति चुनकर पूरा कीजिए:<br>आकृति (X):<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q11.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The pattern is a continuous spiral of black and white bands winding inwards through the hexagon, and the question mark covers the innermost triangular piece.<br>The missing piece must therefore carry the same bands with the same direction and thickness, so that the spiral continues unbroken.<br>Only the piece in option (3) continues the bands correctly; in the other alternatives the bands are reversed, broken or wrongly spaced.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3).</b>","hi":"पैटर्न षट्भुज के भीतर अंदर की ओर लिपटी काली तथा सफेद पट्टियों की एक सतत सर्पिल है, और प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न सबसे भीतरी त्रिभुजाकार भाग को ढकता है।<br>अतः लुप्त भाग में वही पट्टियाँ, उसी दिशा और मोटाई के साथ होनी चाहिए जिससे सर्पिल बिना टूटे आगे बढ़े।<br>केवल विकल्प (3) का भाग पट्टियों को सही ढंग से आगे बढ़ाता है; अन्य विकल्पों में पट्टियाँ उलटी, टूटी हुई या गलत दूरी पर हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q11.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q11_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q11_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q11_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q11_opt4.jpg"]}}},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000071692","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"Which two numbers should be interchanged to make the given equation correct?<br><b>12 ÷ 2 × 4 + 8 − 6 = 14</b> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए समीकरण को सही बनाने के लिए किन दो संख्याओं का आपस में बदला जाना चाहिए?<br><b>12 ÷ 2 × 4 + 8 − 6 = 14</b> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4 and 6","hi":"4 और 6"},"2":{"en":"2 and 4","hi":"2 और 4"},"3":{"en":"6 and 8","hi":"6 और 8"},"4":{"en":"2 and 6","hi":"2 और 6"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Try the interchanges one by one.<br>4 and 6: 12 ÷ 2 × 6 + 8 − 4 = 6 × 6 + 4 = 40 ✗<br>2 and 4: 12 ÷ 4 × 2 + 8 − 6 = 3 × 2 + 2 = 8 ✗<br>6 and 8: 12 ÷ 2 × 4 + 6 − 8 = 24 − 2 = 22 ✗<br>2 and 6: 12 ÷ 6 × 4 + 8 − 2 = 2 × 4 + 8 − 2 = 8 + 8 − 2 = 14 ✓<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 2 and 6.</b>","hi":"एक-एक करके बदलाव जाँचिए।<br>4 तथा 6: 12 ÷ 2 × 6 + 8 − 4 = 6 × 6 + 4 = 40 ✗<br>2 तथा 4: 12 ÷ 4 × 2 + 8 − 6 = 3 × 2 + 2 = 8 ✗<br>6 तथा 8: 12 ÷ 2 × 4 + 6 − 8 = 24 − 2 = 22 ✗<br>2 तथा 6: 12 ÷ 6 × 4 + 8 − 2 = 2 × 4 + 8 − 2 = 8 + 8 − 2 = 14 ✓<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 2 और 6 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000071693","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"If a mirror is placed on the line PQ, which figure will be the mirror image of the question figure?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q13.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि रेखा PQ पर दर्पण स्थापित किया जाए, तो प्रश्न आकृति का दर्पण प्रतिबिंब कौन-सी आकृति होगी?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q13.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The mirror line PQ is vertical, so the combination is reversed from left to right and each character is laterally inverted, while the up-down arrangement stays the same.<br>The rightmost character p comes first, then z, then 4, then 7, then Q and finally m: p z 4 7 Q m, each written as its mirror form.<br>Only option (4) shows this order with all the characters correctly inverted.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4).</b>","hi":"दर्पण रेखा PQ ऊर्ध्वाधर है, इसलिए संयोजन बाएँ से दाएँ उलट जाता है और प्रत्येक अक्षर पार्श्वतः उलटा हो जाता है, जबकि ऊपर-नीचे की व्यवस्था वैसी ही रहती है।<br>सबसे दाईं ओर का अक्षर p पहले आएगा, फिर z, फिर 4, फिर 7, फिर Q और अंत में m: p z 4 7 Q m, प्रत्येक अपने दर्पण रूप में।<br>केवल विकल्प (4) में यही क्रम तथा सभी अक्षर सही रूप से उलटे हुए हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q13.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q13_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q13_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q13_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q13_opt4.jpg"]}}},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000071694","section":"REASONING","topic":"Matrix","question":{"en":"Which of the following rows/columns are connected/related with each other in some way?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\"><b>Rows</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\"><b>I</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\"><b>II</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\"><b>III</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\"><b>IV</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\"><b>V</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">29</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">17</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">31</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">19</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">34</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">22</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">36</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">21</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">25</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">39</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी पंक्तियाँ/स्तंभ किसी न किसी प्रकार एक-दूसरे से जुड़ी/संबंधित हैं?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\"><b>पंक्तियाँ</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\"><b>I</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\"><b>II</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\"><b>III</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\"><b>IV</b></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\"><b>V</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">29</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">17</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">31</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">19</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">34</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">22</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">36</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">21</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">25</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">39</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Columns I, III and IV","hi":"स्तंभ I, III तथा IV"},"2":{"en":"Columns II, IV and V","hi":"स्तंभ II, IV तथा V"},"3":{"en":"Columns I, II and III","hi":"स्तंभ I, II तथा III"},"4":{"en":"Columns II, III and IV","hi":"स्तंभ II, III तथा IV"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Check how the numbers change from row to row in each column.<br>Column I: 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 — increases by 1 each time.<br>Column II: 6, 8, 10, 12, 14 — increases by 2 each time.<br>Column III: 9, 12, 15, 18, 21 — increases by 3 each time.<br>So columns I, II and III have a constant difference down each column (equal to the column number) and are therefore related.<br>Column IV: 14, 17, 19, 22, 25 (differences 3, 2, 3, 3) and column V: 29, 31, 34, 36, 39 (differences 2, 3, 2, 3) show no constant difference.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Columns I, II and III.</b>","hi":"देखिए कि प्रत्येक स्तंभ की संख्याएँ पंक्ति-दर-पंक्ति कैसे बदलती हैं।<br>स्तंभ I: 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 — हर बार 1 से बढ़ती हैं।<br>स्तंभ II: 6, 8, 10, 12, 14 — हर बार 2 से बढ़ती हैं।<br>स्तंभ III: 9, 12, 15, 18, 21 — हर बार 3 से बढ़ती हैं।<br>अतः स्तंभ I, II तथा III में नीचे की ओर अंतर स्थिर है (जो स्तंभ संख्या के बराबर है) और इसलिए ये संबंधित हैं।<br>स्तंभ IV: 14, 17, 19, 22, 25 (अंतर 3, 2, 3, 3) तथा स्तंभ V: 29, 31, 34, 36, 39 (अंतर 2, 3, 2, 3) में कोई स्थिर अंतर नहीं है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): स्तंभ I, II तथा III है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000071695","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"In behavioral psychology, which practice represents the most significant methodological error when interpreting an individual's non-verbal communication and body language? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"व्यवहार-मनोविज्ञान में किसी व्यक्ति के अशाब्दिक संचार तथा शारीरिक भाषा की व्याख्या करते समय कौन-सी कार्यप्रणाली सबसे बड़ी पद्धतिगत त्रुटि मानी जाती है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Isolating specific physical gestures while completely ignoring the situational context","hi":"विशिष्ट शारीरिक हाव-भावों को अलग करके देखना और परिस्थितिजन्य संदर्भ को पूर्णतः अनदेखा करना"},"2":{"en":"Systematically observing baseline behavioral shifts over a prolonged period","hi":"लंबी अवधि में आधारभूत व्यवहारिक परिवर्तनों का व्यवस्थित अवलोकन करना"},"3":{"en":"Asking clarifying questions to verify the individual's true emotional state","hi":"व्यक्ति की वास्तविक भावनात्मक स्थिति की पुष्टि के लिए स्पष्टीकरणात्मक प्रश्न पूछना"},"4":{"en":"Listening closely to verbal responses to check for non-verbal consistency","hi":"अशाब्दिक सुसंगति जाँचने के लिए शाब्दिक उत्तरों को ध्यान से सुनना"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Body language has meaning only in relation to its context: the same gesture (folded arms, avoiding eye contact, fidgeting) can indicate comfort, cold, nervousness or simple habit.<br>Reading a single gesture in isolation, without the situation, the person's baseline behaviour and the accompanying verbal message, is therefore the biggest methodological error, because it invites over-interpretation of normal behaviour.<br>Options (2), (3) and (4) all describe sound practices — observing baseline behaviour over time, verifying interpretations and cross-checking with what the person says.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Isolating specific physical gestures while completely ignoring the situational context.</b>","hi":"शारीरिक भाषा का अर्थ केवल उसके संदर्भ के साथ ही होता है: एक ही हाव-भाव (हाथ बाँधना, नज़र चुराना, बेचैनी) सहजता, ठंड, घबराहट या केवल आदत का संकेत हो सकता है।<br>इसलिए किसी एक हाव-भाव को परिस्थिति, व्यक्ति के सामान्य व्यवहार तथा साथ के शाब्दिक संदेश से अलग करके देखना ही सबसे बड़ी पद्धतिगत त्रुटि है, क्योंकि इससे सामान्य व्यवहार का अतिव्याख्या होने लगती है।<br>विकल्प (2), (3) तथा (4) सभी उचित कार्यप्रणालियाँ बताते हैं — समय के साथ सामान्य व्यवहार का अवलोकन, व्याख्या की पुष्टि तथा व्यक्ति के कथन से मिलान।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): विशिष्ट शारीरिक हाव-भावों को अलग करके देखना और परिस्थितिजन्य संदर्भ को पूर्णतः अनदेखा करना है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000071696","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Find the figure that does NOT match the others.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q16.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वह आकृति खोजिए जो अन्य आकृतियों से मेल नहीं खाती।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q16.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A"},"2":{"en":"B"},"3":{"en":"C"},"4":{"en":"D"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Count the small shaded squares in each figure.<br>Figure (A) is made of 4 small squares, figure (B) of 4 small squares and figure (D) of 4 small squares (2 × 2).<br>Figure (C), however, is made of 5 small squares, so it does not match the other three.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): C.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक आकृति में छोटे छायांकित वर्गों की गिनती कीजिए।<br>आकृति (A) 4 छोटे वर्गों से, आकृति (B) 4 छोटे वर्गों से तथा आकृति (D) 4 छोटे वर्गों (2 × 2) से बनी है।<br>परंतु आकृति (C) 5 छोटे वर्गों से बनी है, इसलिए यह अन्य तीन से मेल नहीं खाती।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): C है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q16.jpg"]}},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000071697","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Analyse the provided figures and choose the one that is different from the rest.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q17.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई आकृतियों का विश्लेषण कीजिए और वह आकृति चुनिए जो शेष से भिन्न है।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q17.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A"},"2":{"en":"B"},"3":{"en":"C"},"4":{"en":"D"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Each figure shows a small two-wheeled cart with two shapes drawn on its body.<br>In figures (A), (C) and (D) the two shapes on the body are identical to each other — two pentagons, two squares and two circles respectively.<br>In figure (B) the two shapes are different (a triangle and a circle), so it is the odd one out.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): B.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक आकृति में दो पहियों वाली एक छोटी गाड़ी है, जिसके ऊपरी भाग पर दो आकृतियाँ बनी हैं।<br>आकृतियों (A), (C) तथा (D) में गाड़ी पर बनी दोनों आकृतियाँ एक-दूसरे जैसी हैं — क्रमशः दो पंचभुज, दो वर्ग तथा दो वृत्त।<br>आकृति (B) में दोनों आकृतियाँ भिन्न हैं (एक त्रिभुज तथा एक वृत्त), इसलिए यही विषम है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): B है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q17.jpg"]}},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000071698","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, there is a specific relationship between the first two figures. Establish a similar relationship between the third and fourth figures by selecting a suitable figure from the given Answer Figures to replace the question mark (?).<br><b>Question Figures:</b><br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q18.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में पहली दो आकृतियों के बीच एक निश्चित संबंध है। तीसरी तथा चौथी आकृति के बीच भी वही संबंध स्थापित कीजिए और प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर उपयुक्त उत्तर आकृति चुनिए।<br><b>प्रश्न आकृतियाँ:</b><br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q18.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"3"},"3":{"en":"5"},"4":{"en":"2"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"From the first figure to the second, the open half-circle is closed into a complete circle and the upper half of this completed figure is shaded black while the lower half remains white.<br>Applying the same change to the third figure — completing the open shape symmetrically and filling its upper part black — gives the figure shown as answer figure (3).<br>In the other answer figures the shading is on the wrong side or the shape is not completed in the same way.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 3.</b>","hi":"पहली आकृति से दूसरी आकृति में खुला अर्धवृत्त पूर्ण वृत्त में बदल जाता है और इस पूर्ण आकृति का ऊपरी आधा भाग काला भर दिया जाता है, जबकि निचला आधा भाग सफेद रहता है।<br>यही परिवर्तन तीसरी आकृति पर लागू करने पर — खुली आकृति को सममित रूप से पूरा करके उसका ऊपरी भाग काला भरने पर — उत्तर आकृति (3) प्राप्त होती है।<br>अन्य उत्तर आकृतियों में छायांकन गलत ओर है या आकृति उसी प्रकार पूरी नहीं की गई है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q18.jpg"]}},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000071699","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, there is a specific relationship between the first two figures. Establish a similar relationship between the third and fourth figures by selecting a suitable figure from the given Answer Figures to replace the question mark (?).<br><b>Question Figures:</b><br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q19.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में पहली दो आकृतियों के बीच एक निश्चित संबंध है। तीसरी तथा चौथी आकृति के बीच भी वही संबंध स्थापित कीजिए और प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर उपयुक्त उत्तर आकृति चुनिए।<br><b>प्रश्न आकृतियाँ:</b><br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q19.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"From the first figure to the second, one chevron-shaped mark is added above the head of the stick figure and the number of chevrons on the trunk decreases by one (4 → 3).<br>Applying the same change to the third figure, which has 5 chevrons on the trunk, gives a figure with a chevron above the head and 4 chevrons on the trunk — exactly answer figure (3).<br>Answer figures (1), (2), (4) and (5) either keep the wrong number of chevrons on the trunk or replace the mark above the head by a bracket.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 3.</b>","hi":"पहली आकृति से दूसरी आकृति में मानव-आकृति के सिर के ऊपर एक कोण (शेवरॉन) चिह्न जोड़ दिया जाता है तथा धड़ पर बने कोणों की संख्या एक घट जाती है (4 → 3)।<br>यही परिवर्तन तीसरी आकृति पर लागू करने पर, जिसके धड़ पर 5 कोण हैं, सिर के ऊपर एक कोण तथा धड़ पर 4 कोण वाली आकृति प्राप्त होती है — ठीक उत्तर आकृति (3)।<br>उत्तर आकृतियों (1), (2), (4) तथा (5) में या तो धड़ पर कोणों की संख्या गलत है या सिर के ऊपर का चिह्न कोष्ठक से बदल दिया गया है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q19.jpg"]}},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000071700","section":"REASONING","topic":"Embedded Figures","question":{"en":"Carefully observe Figure (X) and identify the answer figure in which Figure (X) is embedded in the same or rotated form.<br><b>Figure X:</b><br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q20.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"आकृति (X) को ध्यानपूर्वक देखिए और वह उत्तर आकृति पहचानिए जिसमें आकृति (X) उसी रूप में अथवा घूर्णित रूप में अंतर्निहित है।<br><b>आकृति X:</b><br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q20.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"3"},"3":{"en":"4"},"4":{"en":"1"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Figure (X) is the letter F drawn with three straight lines — a long vertical line, a horizontal line at the top and a shorter horizontal line in the middle.<br>In answer figure (2) the square is divided by diagonals and sides in such a way that these three lines of the letter F appear inside it in rotated form.<br>In answer figure (1) the diagonals never combine to give two parallel horizontals meeting a vertical, and in (3) and (4) the required vertical line with two one-sided horizontals is absent.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2.</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) अक्षर F है, जो तीन सीधी रेखाओं से बना है — एक लंबी ऊर्ध्वाधर रेखा, ऊपर की ओर एक क्षैतिज रेखा तथा बीच में एक छोटी क्षैतिज रेखा।<br>उत्तर आकृति (2) के वर्ग में विकर्ण तथा भुजाएँ इस प्रकार बनी हैं कि अक्षर F की ये तीनों रेखाएँ घूर्णित रूप में उसके भीतर दिखाई देती हैं।<br>उत्तर आकृति (1) में विकर्ण मिलकर एक ऊर्ध्वाधर रेखा के साथ दो समांतर क्षैतिज रेखाएँ नहीं बनाते, तथा (3) और (4) में अभीष्ट ऊर्ध्वाधर रेखा के साथ एक ही ओर की दो क्षैतिज रेखाएँ नहीं हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q20.jpg"]}},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000071701","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"Select a figure from amongst the alternatives that will continue the same series as established by the problem figures.<br><b>Problem Figures:</b><br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q21.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उन विकल्पों में से वह आकृति चुनिए जो प्रश्न आकृतियों द्वारा स्थापित उसी श्रेणी को आगे बढ़ाए।<br><b>प्रश्न आकृतियाँ:</b><br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q21.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The boxes contain the symbols of a triangle, a cross and an equals sign arranged in a single row.<br>From one figure to the next, every symbol shifts one place to the left and the leftmost symbol goes round to the right end: (triangle, ×, =) → (×, =, triangle) → (=, triangle, ×).<br>Continuing the same cyclic left shift, the next figure must be (triangle, ×, =), which is exactly the arrangement in option (3).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3).</b>","hi":"बक्सों में त्रिभुज, क्रॉस तथा बराबर के चिह्न एक ही पंक्ति में व्यवस्थित हैं।<br>एक आकृति से अगली आकृति में प्रत्येक चिह्न एक स्थान बाईं ओर खिसक जाता है और सबसे बायाँ चिह्न दाईं ओर के अंत में चला जाता है: (त्रिभुज, ×, =) → (×, =, त्रिभुज) → (=, त्रिभुज, ×)।<br>यही चक्रीय बाएँ खिसकाव जारी रखने पर अगली आकृति (त्रिभुज, ×, =) होनी चाहिए, जो ठीक विकल्प (3) में है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q21.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q21_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q21_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q21_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q21_opt4.jpg"]}}},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000071702","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"Read the given situation carefully and consider all the relevant facts, conditions and constraints. Choose the option that represents the most appropriate, practical and logical decision based solely on the information provided.<br><br>A logistics firm promotes delivery supervisors if they have completed 2 years of service, have zero active customer complaints and have an attendance rate above 95%. Nitin has worked with the firm for 3 years, has an attendance rate of 97%, but has 1 active customer complaint registered against him last month.<br><br>What decision should be taken? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई परिस्थिति को ध्यानपूर्वक पढ़िए तथा सभी संबंधित तथ्यों, शर्तों और प्रतिबंधों पर विचार कीजिए। वह विकल्प चुनिए जो केवल दी गई जानकारी के आधार पर सबसे उपयुक्त, व्यावहारिक तथा तार्किक निर्णय दर्शाता है।<br><br>एक लॉजिस्टिक्स कंपनी डिलीवरी सुपरवाइज़रों को पदोन्नति तब देती है जब उन्होंने 2 वर्ष की सेवा पूरी कर ली हो, उनके विरुद्ध ग्राहक शिकायत सक्रिय न हो तथा उपस्थिति दर 95% से अधिक हो। नितिन ने कंपनी के साथ 3 वर्ष कार्य किया है, उसकी उपस्थिति दर 97% है, किंतु पिछले महीने उसके विरुद्ध 1 सक्रिय ग्राहक शिकायत दर्ज हुई है।<br><br>क्या निर्णय लिया जाना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The candidate should be rejected for promotion.","hi":"अभ्यर्थी को पदोन्नति के लिए अस्वीकार किया जाना चाहिए।"},"2":{"en":"The candidate should be selected for promotion.","hi":"अभ्यर्थी को पदोन्नति के लिए चुना जाना चाहिए।"},"3":{"en":"The application should be referred to the Director.","hi":"आवेदन निदेशक को निर्दिष्ट किया जाना चाहिए।"},"4":{"en":"The data provided is inadequate to take a decision.","hi":"निर्णय लेने के लिए दी गई जानकारी अपर्याप्त है।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The conditions for promotion are cumulative: service of at least 2 years, zero active customer complaints and attendance above 95%.<br>Nitin satisfies the service condition (3 years) and the attendance condition (97%), but he fails the condition of having zero active complaints, because one complaint is still registered against him.<br>Since even one active complaint disqualifies a candidate, his application must be rejected; nothing in the data is missing and no referral to a higher authority is warranted.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The candidate should be rejected for promotion.</b>","hi":"पदोन्नति की शर्तें संचयी हैं: कम से कम 2 वर्ष की सेवा, कोई सक्रिय ग्राहक शिकायत न होना तथा 95% से अधिक उपस्थिति।<br>नितिन सेवा की शर्त (3 वर्ष) तथा उपस्थिति की शर्त (97%) पूरी करता है, किंतु शून्य सक्रिय शिकायत की शर्त पूरी नहीं करता, क्योंकि उसके विरुद्ध एक शिकायत अभी सक्रिय है।<br>एक भी सक्रिय शिकायत अभ्यर्थी को अपात्र बना देती है, अतः उसका आवेदन अस्वीकार किया जाना चाहिए; जानकारी में कोई कमी नहीं है और उच्च अधिकारी को निर्दिष्ट करने का कोई कारण नहीं है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): अभ्यर्थी को पदोन्नति के लिए अस्वीकार किया जाना चाहिए।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000071703","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Find the missing term (?) in the following series.<br><b>Warm → Hot → Scorching → ?</b> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित श्रेणी में लुप्त पद (?) ज्ञात कीजिए।<br><b>Warm → Hot → Scorching → ?</b> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Burning","hi":"Burning (जलता हुआ)"},"2":{"en":"Mild","hi":"Mild (हल्का)"},"3":{"en":"Tepid","hi":"Tepid (कुनकुना)"},"4":{"en":"Cool","hi":"Cool (ठंडा)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"All the words describe the degree of heat, and they are arranged in increasing order of intensity:<br>warm (slightly hot) → hot → scorching (burning the skin) → ?<br>The next and most intense stage in this order is 'burning', which continues the same increasing sequence.<br>Mild, tepid and cool all move in the opposite direction and would come before 'warm'.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Burning.</b>","hi":"सभी शब्द गर्मी की मात्रा बताते हैं और वे बढ़ती तीव्रता के क्रम में रखे गए हैं:<br>warm (थोड़ा गर्म) → hot → scorching (झुलसाने वाला) → ?<br>इसी क्रम का अगला तथा सर्वाधिक तीव्र स्तर 'burning' है, जो इस बढ़ती श्रेणी को आगे बढ़ाता है।<br>Mild, tepid तथा cool सभी विपरीत दिशा में जाते हैं और 'warm' से पहले आएँगे।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): Burning है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000071704","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Which pair shares the SAME type of relationship as <b>COMPOSER : SYMPHONY</b>? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किस युग्म में वही संबंध है जो <b>COMPOSER : SYMPHONY</b> में है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Author : Novel","hi":"रचयिता (Author) : उपन्यास (Novel)"},"2":{"en":"Singer : Microphone","hi":"गायक (Singer) : माइक्रोफ़ोन (Microphone)"},"3":{"en":"Painter : Canvas","hi":"चित्रकार (Painter) : कैनवास (Canvas)"},"4":{"en":"Chef : Kitchen","hi":"रसोइया (Chef) : रसोई (Kitchen)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"A composer creates a symphony — the first word is the creator and the second word is the work he creates.<br>Author : Novel ✓ (an author creates a novel)<br>Singer : Microphone ✗ (a tool used while singing, not a creation)<br>Painter : Canvas ✗ (canvas is the material on which he paints, not the finished work)<br>Chef : Kitchen ✗ (a place of work)<br>So only the first pair has the same creator-and-creature relationship.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Author : Novel.</b>","hi":"संगीतकार (composer) एक सिम्फनी रचता है — पहला शब्द रचनाकार है और दूसरा शब्द उसकी रचना।<br>रचयिता : उपन्यास ✓ (रचयिता उपन्यास रचता है)<br>गायक : माइक्रोफ़ोन ✗ (यह गाने में प्रयुक्त साधन है, रचना नहीं)<br>चित्रकार : कैनवास ✗ (कैनवास वह सामग्री है जिस पर चित्र बनाया जाता है, तैयार कृति नहीं)<br>रसोइया : रसोई ✗ (कार्यस्थल)<br>अतः केवल पहले युग्म में रचनाकार और रचना का संबंध है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): रचयिता : उपन्यास है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000071705","section":"REASONING","topic":"Dice & Cube","question":{"en":"If a cube is made using the given arrangement, which of the Answer Figures will be correct?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q25.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि दी गई व्यवस्था से एक घन बनाया जाए, तो कौन-सी उत्तर आकृति सही होगी?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q25.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A"},"2":{"en":"B"},"3":{"en":"C"},"4":{"en":"D"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Fold the net into a cube and note which faces become adjacent and which become opposite.<br>The face with one circle and the face with four circles lie on opposite sides of the net, so they can never be seen together; likewise the face with two circles and the face with three circles, and the two remaining faces with three circles, are opposite pairs.<br>Checking each answer figure with these pairs: in (A), (C) and (D) two faces that are opposite in the net appear together, whereas answer figure (B) shows only faces that really meet at a corner, with the correct number of circles and in the correct relative position.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): B.</b>","hi":"जाल (net) को मोड़कर घन बनाइए और देखिए कौन-से फलक पास-पास आते हैं तथा कौन-से आमने-सामने।<br>एक वृत्त वाला फलक तथा चार वृत्त वाला फलक जाल में आमने-सामने पड़ते हैं, इसलिए वे कभी साथ नहीं दिख सकते; इसी प्रकार दो वृत्त वाला फलक तथा तीन वृत्त वाला फलक, और शेष दो तीन-वृत्त वाले फलक भी विपरीत युग्म हैं।<br>इन युग्मों से प्रत्येक उत्तर आकृति जाँचने पर: (A), (C) तथा (D) में जाल में विपरीत फलक साथ दिखाए गए हैं, जबकि उत्तर आकृति (B) में केवल वही फलक हैं जो वास्तव में एक कोने पर मिलते हैं, वृत्तों की सही संख्या तथा सही सापेक्ष स्थिति के साथ।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): B है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q25.jpg"]}}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000071706","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Microeconomics","question":{"en":"Who among the following economists explained the substitution and the income effect? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से किस अर्थशास्त्री ने प्रतिस्थापन तथा आय प्रभाव की व्याख्या की? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Hicks and Allen","hi":"हिक्स तथा एलन"},"2":{"en":"Lionel Robbins","hi":"लियोनेल रॉबिन्स"},"3":{"en":"Ursula Webb","hi":"अर्सुला वेब"},"4":{"en":"Abba Lerner","hi":"अब्बा लर्नर"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Hicks and Allen</b><br><b>J.R. Hicks and R.G.D. Allen</b> (1934) developed the <b>indifference curve</b> technique and split the price effect into the <b>substitution effect and the income effect</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>substitution effect</b> is the change in quantity demanded due to a change in relative prices, while the <b>income effect</b> is the change due to a change in real income.<br>• Hicks and Allen showed that these effects can be separated through <b>compensating variation</b> using indifference curves.<br>• <b>Lionel Robbins</b> gave the scarcity-centred definition of economics in his 1932 essay.<br>• <b>Abba Lerner</b> developed the Lerner Index of monopoly power, and <b>Ursula Webb</b> is associated with the Webbs' work on trade unions.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because the substitution and income effects were explained by Hicks and Allen.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – हिक्स तथा एलन</b><br><b>जे. आर. हिक्स तथा आर. जी. डी. एलन</b> (1934) ने <b>उदासीनता वक्र (Indifference curve)</b> तकनीक विकसित की और कीमत प्रभाव को <b>प्रतिस्थापन प्रभाव तथा आय प्रभाव</b> में विभाजित किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>प्रतिस्थापन प्रभाव (Substitution effect)</b> सापेक्ष कीमतों में परिवर्तन से माँगी गई मात्रा में परिवर्तन है, जबकि <b>आय प्रभाव (Income effect)</b> वास्तविक आय में परिवर्तन से होने वाला परिवर्तन है।<br>• हिक्स तथा एलन ने उदासीनता वक्रों के माध्यम से <b>क्षतिपूरक विचलन (Compensating variation)</b> द्वारा इन प्रभावों को अलग दिखाया।<br>• <b>लियोनेल रॉबिन्स</b> ने 1932 के अपने निबंध में अर्थशास्त्र की दुर्लभता-केंद्रित परिभाषा दी।<br>• <b>अब्बा लर्नर</b> ने एकाधिकार शक्ति का लर्नर सूचकांक विकसित किया, तथा <b>अर्सुला वेब</b> का नाम ट्रेड यूनियन पर वेब्स के कार्य से जुड़ा है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि प्रतिस्थापन तथा आय प्रभाव की व्याख्या हिक्स एवं एलन ने की।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000071707","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: The Mughal Empire","question":{"en":"The concept of Sulh-i-Kul (peace for all) was most systematically implemented under which Mughal emperor? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"'सुल्ह-ए-कुल' (सबके लिए शांति) की अवधारणा किस मुगल सम्राट के अंतर्गत सर्वाधिक व्यवस्थित रूप से लागू की गई? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Babur","hi":"बाबर"},"2":{"en":"Humayun","hi":"हुमायूँ"},"3":{"en":"Akbar","hi":"अकबर"},"4":{"en":"Aurangzeb","hi":"औरंगज़ेब"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Akbar</b><br><b>Sulh-i-Kul</b>, literally 'peace with all', was the core policy of <b>Akbar</b>, who applied it through the <b>Din-i-Ilahi</b>, the Ibadat Khana debates, the abolition of the jizya and the appointment of Hindus to high offices.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The idea was shaped by Akbar's tutor <b>Abul Fazl</b>, who explained it in the <b>Akbarnama</b> and <b>Ain-i-Akbari</b>.<br>• Akbar abolished the <b>jizya</b> in 1564 and the pilgrimage tax, and issued the <b>Mazhar</b> (infallibility decree) in 1579.<br>• <b>Jahangir</b> continued the policy in practice, but <b>Aurangzeb</b> reversed it by reimposing the jizya in 1679.<br>• <b>Babur</b> and <b>Humayun</b> ruled before the policy took shape, so they cannot be credited with its systematic implementation.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because Sulh-i-Kul was most systematically implemented under Akbar.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अकबर</b><br><b>सुल्ह-ए-कुल (Sulh-i-Kul)</b> अर्थात् 'सबके साथ शांति' <b>अकबर</b> की मूल नीति थी, जिसे उन्होंने <b>दीन-ए-इलाही</b>, इबादत खाना की चर्चाओं, जजिया के उन्मूलन तथा हिंदुओं को उच्च पदों पर नियुक्ति के माध्यम से लागू किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इस विचार को अकबर के शिक्षक <b>अबुल फजल</b> ने आकार दिया, जिन्होंने इसे <b>अकबरनामा</b> तथा <b>आइन-ए-अकबरी</b> में समझाया।<br>• अकबर ने 1564 में <b>जजिया</b> तथा तीर्थ-यात्रा कर हटाया और 1579 में <b>मजहर</b> (अचूकता का फरमान) जारी किया।<br>• <b>जहाँगीर</b> ने व्यवहार में इस नीति को जारी रखा, परंतु <b>औरंगज़ेब</b> ने 1679 में जजिया पुनः लगाकर इसे उलट दिया।<br>• <b>बाबर</b> तथा <b>हुमायूँ</b> ने इस नीति के विकसित होने से पहले शासन किया, इसलिए उन्हें इसके व्यवस्थित क्रियान्वयन का श्रेय नहीं दिया जा सकता।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि सुल्ह-ए-कुल सर्वाधिक व्यवस्थित रूप से अकबर के अंतर्गत लागू हुई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000071708","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Himalayan River System","question":{"en":"Which of the following rivers flows through Pakistan and India? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी नदी पाकिस्तान तथा भारत दोनों से होकर बहती है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Indus River","hi":"सिंधु नदी"},"2":{"en":"Ganges River","hi":"गंगा नदी"},"3":{"en":"Brahmaputra River","hi":"ब्रह्मपुत्र नदी"},"4":{"en":"Kabul River","hi":"काबुल नदी"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Indus River</b><br>The <b>Indus</b> rises in Tibet near Lake Mansarovar, enters India through Ladakh and flows through Pakistan to drain into the Arabian Sea, so it flows through both India and Pakistan.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Indus is about <b>3,180 km</b> long and is called the 'lifeline of Pakistan'; its five tributaries in Punjab are the Jhelum, Chenab, Ravi, Beas and Sutlej.<br>• Under the <b>Indus Waters Treaty, 1960</b>, India controls the eastern rivers (Ravi, Beas, Sutlej) and Pakistan the western rivers.<br>• The <b>Ganges</b> and the <b>Brahmaputra</b> flow through India and Bangladesh, not Pakistan.<br>• The <b>Kabul River</b> flows from Afghanistan into Pakistan and joins the Indus; it does not enter India.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because among the given rivers only the Indus flows through both countries.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – सिंधु नदी</b><br><b>सिंधु नदी</b> तिब्बत में मानसरोवर झील के निकट से निकलती है, लद्दाख से भारत में प्रवेश करती है और पाकिस्तान से होकर अरब सागर में गिरती है, इसलिए यह भारत तथा पाकिस्तान दोनों से बहती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सिंधु नदी लगभग <b>3,180 किमी</b> लंबी है और इसे 'पाकिस्तान की जीवनरेखा' कहा जाता है; पंजाब में इसकी पाँच सहायक नदियाँ झेलम, चिनाब, रावी, ब्यास तथा सतलुज हैं।<br>• <b>सिंधु जल संधि, 1960</b> के अंतर्गत पूर्वी नदियाँ (रावी, ब्यास, सतलुज) भारत के तथा पश्चिमी नदियाँ पाकिस्तान के नियंत्रण में हैं।<br>• <b>गंगा</b> तथा <b>ब्रह्मपुत्र</b> भारत और बांग्लादेश से होकर बहती हैं, पाकिस्तान से नहीं।<br>• <b>काबुल नदी</b> अफगानिस्तान से पाकिस्तान में बहकर सिंधु में मिलती है; यह भारत में प्रवेश नहीं करती।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि दी गई नदियों में केवल सिंधु दोनों देशों से बहती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000071709","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Government Schemes","question":{"en":"Which government initiative primarily focuses on enhancing skill development and vocational training opportunities for the youth in India? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सी सरकारी पहल भारत में युवाओं के लिए कौशल विकास तथा व्यावसायिक प्रशिक्षण के अवसरों को बढ़ाने पर मुख्य रूप से केंद्रित है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Startup India","hi":"स्टार्टअप इंडिया"},"2":{"en":"Make in India","hi":"मेक इन इंडिया"},"3":{"en":"Skill India Mission","hi":"स्किल इंडिया मिशन"},"4":{"en":"National Education Policy (NEP) 2020","hi":"राष्ट्रीय शिक्षा नीति (एनईपी) 2020"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Skill India Mission</b><br>The <b>Skill India Mission</b>, launched on 15 July 2015, works through <b>Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY)</b> and the National Skill Development Corporation to give youth industry-relevant skill training and certification.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Skill India is run by the <b>Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepreneurship</b>, created in 2014; its target is to skill a large section of the workforce.<br>• PMKVY provides <b>short-term training, recognition of prior learning and stipend support</b> for certification.<br>• <b>Startup India</b> supports new enterprises and <b>Make in India</b> promotes manufacturing; neither is primarily a skilling programme.<br>• <b>NEP 2020</b> is an education policy that also promotes vocational education, but the dedicated skilling mission is Skill India.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because skill development and vocational training for youth is the core objective of the Skill India Mission.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – स्किल इंडिया मिशन</b><br>15 जुलाई 2015 को शुरू किया गया <b>स्किल इंडिया मिशन</b> <b>प्रधानमंत्री कौशल विकास योजना (PMKVY)</b> तथा राष्ट्रीय कौशल विकास निगम के माध्यम से युवाओं को उद्योग-उपयोगी कौशल प्रशिक्षण एवं प्रमाणन देता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• स्किल इंडिया <b>कौशल विकास एवं उद्यमिता मंत्रालय</b> द्वारा संचालित है, जिसका गठन 2014 में हुआ; इसका लक्ष्य कार्यबल के बड़े भाग को कुशल बनाना है।<br>• PMKVY <b>अल्पकालिक प्रशिक्षण, पूर्व अधिगम की मान्यता तथा प्रमाणन हेतु वजीफा</b> प्रदान करता है।<br>• <b>स्टार्टअप इंडिया</b> नए उद्यमों को सहायता देता है और <b>मेक इन इंडिया</b> विनिर्माण को बढ़ावा देता है; इनमें से कोई मुख्य रूप से कौशल कार्यक्रम नहीं है।<br>• <b>एनईपी 2020</b> शिक्षा नीति है जो व्यावसायिक शिक्षा को भी बढ़ावा देती है, परंतु समर्पित कौशल मिशन स्किल इंडिया है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि युवाओं के कौशल विकास एवं व्यावसायिक प्रशिक्षण का मुख्य उद्देश्य स्किल इंडिया मिशन का है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000071710","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Government Schemes","question":{"en":"The \"Swachh Bharat Mission\" has two main components: Swachh Bharat Mission (Gramin) and Swachh Bharat Mission (Urban). What is the primary objective of the Swachh Bharat Mission (Gramin)? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"\"स्वच्छ भारत मिशन\" के दो मुख्य घटक हैं: स्वच्छ भारत मिशन (ग्रामीण) तथा स्वच्छ भारत मिशन (शहरी)। स्वच्छ भारत मिशन (ग्रामीण) का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To improve the air quality in rural areas through pollution control measures.","hi":"प्रदूषण नियंत्रण उपायों के माध्यम से ग्रामीण क्षेत्रों में वायु गुणवत्ता में सुधार करना।"},"2":{"en":"To achieve Open Defecation Free (ODF) status and improve solid and liquid waste management in rural India.","hi":"खुले में शौच से मुक्त (ODF) दर्जा प्राप्त करना तथा ग्रामीण भारत में ठोस एवं तरल अपशिष्ट प्रबंधन में सुधार करना।"},"3":{"en":"To provide access to clean drinking water to all rural households.","hi":"सभी ग्रामीण परिवारों को स्वच्छ पेयजल उपलब्ध कराना।"},"4":{"en":"To promote digital literacy and access to online services in rural communities.","hi":"ग्रामीण समुदायों में डिजिटल साक्षरता तथा ऑनलाइन सेवाओं तक पहुँच को बढ़ावा देना।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – To achieve Open Defecation Free (ODF) status and improve solid and liquid waste management in rural India.</b><br>The primary objective of <b>Swachh Bharat Mission (Gramin)</b> is to make villages <b>Open Defecation Free</b>, build individual household toilets and improve <b>solid and liquid waste management</b> in rural areas.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• SBM was launched on <b>2 October 2014</b>; SBM (Gramin) is run by the <b>Ministry of Jal Shakti</b> (earlier Drinking Water and Sanitation) and SBM (Urban) by the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs.<br>• SBM-Gramin entered its <b>second phase (2020-25)</b> with the goal of ODF Plus, covering grey water and plastic waste management.<br>• Rural drinking water is the subject of <b>Jal Jeevan Mission</b>, and air pollution control does not fall under SBM.<br>• <b>Digital literacy</b> is promoted by schemes like PMGDISHA, not by SBM.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because ODF status and waste management are the chief aims of SBM (Gramin).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – खुले में शौच से मुक्त (ODF) दर्जा प्राप्त करना तथा ग्रामीण भारत में ठोस एवं तरल अपशिष्ट प्रबंधन में सुधार करना।</b><br><b>स्वच्छ भारत मिशन (ग्रामीण)</b> का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य गाँवों को <b>खुले में शौच से मुक्त (Open Defecation Free)</b> बनाना, व्यक्तिगत शौचालय बनवाना तथा ग्रामीण क्षेत्रों में <b>ठोस एवं तरल अपशिष्ट प्रबंधन</b> में सुधार करना है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• SBM की शुरुआत <b>2 अक्टूबर 2014</b> को हुई; SBM (ग्रामीण) <b>जल शक्ति मंत्रालय</b> (पूर्व में पेयजल एवं स्वच्छता) तथा SBM (शहरी) आवास एवं शहरी कार्य मंत्रालय द्वारा संचालित होता है।<br>• SBM-ग्रामीण का <b>दूसरा चरण (2020-25)</b> ODF प्लस के लक्ष्य के साथ शुरू हुआ, जिसमें ग्रे वाटर तथा प्लास्टिक अपशिष्ट प्रबंधन सम्मिलित है।<br>• ग्रामीण पेयजल <b>जल जीवन मिशन</b> का विषय है, तथा वायु प्रदूषण नियंत्रण SBM के अंतर्गत नहीं आता।<br>• <b>डिजिटल साक्षरता</b> को PMGDISHA जैसी योजनाओं से बढ़ावा दिया जाता है, SBM से नहीं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि ODF दर्जा तथा अपशिष्ट प्रबंधन SBM (ग्रामीण) के मुख्य लक्ष्य हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000071711","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"The 2014 Lusofonia Games, a multi-sport event for Portuguese-speaking countries, were held in which Indian city? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"2014 का लुसोफ़ोनिया खेल (Lusofonia Games), जो पुर्तगाली भाषी देशों का बहु-खेल आयोजन है, भारत के किस शहर में हुआ था? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mumbai","hi":"मुंबई"},"2":{"en":"Chennai","hi":"चेन्नई"},"3":{"en":"Kolkata","hi":"कोलकाता"},"4":{"en":"Goa","hi":"गोवा"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Goa</b><br>The <b>2014 Lusofonia Games</b>, the multi-sport event for Portuguese-speaking countries, were held in <b>Goa</b> from 18 to 29 January 2014, with the opening ceremony at Fatorda Stadium.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It was the <b>3rd edition</b> of the Lusofonia Games, organised by ACOLOP, and India hosted it because of Goa's Portuguese colonial heritage.<br>• Around 7,000 athletes from 12 countries participated across sports such as athletics, football, volleyball, table tennis and wushu.<br>• Goa was a Portuguese colony until <b>1961</b>, when it was liberated by Operation Vijay and became a Union Territory, attaining statehood in 1987.<br>• The Lusofonia Games were earlier held in Macau (2006) and Lisbon (2009).<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because the 2014 Lusofonia Games were held in Goa.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – गोवा</b><br>पुर्तगाली भाषी देशों का बहु-खेल आयोजन <b>2014 लुसोफ़ोनिया खेल (Lusofonia Games)</b> <b>गोवा</b> में 18 से 29 जनवरी 2014 तक हुए, जिनका उद्घाटन समारोह फातोर्डा स्टेडियम में हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह लुसोफ़ोनिया खेलों का <b>तीसरा संस्करण</b> था, जिसे ACOLOP द्वारा आयोजित किया गया और गोवा की पुर्तगाली औपनिवेशिक विरासत के कारण भारत को आयोजन मिला।<br>• एथलेटिक्स, फुटबॉल, वॉलीबॉल, टेबल टेनिस तथा वुशू जैसे खेलों में 12 देशों के लगभग 7,000 खिलाड़ियों ने भाग लिया।<br>• गोवा <b>1961</b> तक पुर्तगाली उपनिवेश था, जब ऑपरेशन विजय से मुक्त हुआ और केंद्रशासित प्रदेश बना; 1987 में इसे राज्य का दर्जा मिला।<br>• लुसोफ़ोनिया खेल पूर्व में मकाउ (2006) तथा लिस्बन (2009) में हुए थे।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि 2014 के लुसोफ़ोनिया खेल गोवा में हुए।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000071712","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Books and Authors","question":{"en":"Who became the first Arabic-language writer to win the International Booker Prize in 2019? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"2019 में अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बुकर पुरस्कार जीतने वाला पहला अरबी भाषा का लेखक कौन बना? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Hoda Barakat","hi":"होदा बरकत"},"2":{"en":"Naguib Mahfouz","hi":"नजीब महफूज़"},"3":{"en":"Jokha Alharthi","hi":"जोखा अलहार्थी"},"4":{"en":"Adania Shibli","hi":"अदनिया शिबली"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Jokha Alharthi</b><br><b>Jokha Alharthi</b> from Oman won the International Booker Prize in 2019 for <b>Celestial Bodies</b>, translated by Marilyn Booth, becoming the first Arabic-language writer to win the award.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The International Booker Prize is given for a book <b>translated into English</b>, and the prize money is shared equally between the author and the translator.<br>• <b>Celestial Bodies</b> (Arabic: Sayyidat al-Qamar) traces three generations of an Omani family.<br>• <b>Naguib Mahfouz</b> was the first Arabic writer to win the <b>Nobel Prize in Literature</b> (1988), which is a different award.<br>• <b>Hoda Barakat</b> is a Lebanese novelist and <b>Adania Shibli</b> a Palestinian writer; both have been shortlisted for international prizes but not won the International Booker.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because Jokha Alharthi was the first Arabic-language International Booker winner.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – जोखा अलहार्थी</b><br>ओमान की <b>जोखा अलहार्थी (Jokha Alharthi)</b> ने मैरिलिन बूथ द्वारा अनूदित <b>Celestial Bodies</b> के लिए 2019 का अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बुकर पुरस्कार जीता और यह पुरस्कार जीतने वाली पहली अरबी भाषा की लेखिका बनीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बुकर पुरस्कार <b>अंग्रेज़ी में अनूदित</b> पुस्तक को दिया जाता है तथा पुरस्कार राशि लेखक और अनुवादक में समान रूप से बाँटी जाती है।<br>• <b>Celestial Bodies</b> (अरबी: सय्यिदात अल-कमर) एक ओमानी परिवार की तीन पीढ़ियों की कथा है।<br>• <b>नजीब महफूज़</b> <b>साहित्य के नोबेल पुरस्कार</b> (1988) जीतने वाले पहले अरबी लेखक थे, जो भिन्न पुरस्कार है।<br>• <b>होदा बरकत</b> लेबनानी उपन्यासकार तथा <b>अदनिया शिबली</b> फिलिस्तीनी लेखिका हैं; दोनों अंतर्राष्ट्रीय पुरस्कारों के लिए चयनित रही हैं, परंतु अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बुकर नहीं जीता।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि जोखा अलहार्थी पहली अरबी भाषी अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बुकर विजेता थीं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000071713","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Awards and Honours","question":{"en":"Who among the following Indians is not a recipient of the Ramon Magsaysay Award? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित भारतीयों में से कौन रेमन मैग्सेसे पुरस्कार प्राप्तकर्ता नहीं है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Sanjiv Chaturvedi","hi":"संजीव चतुर्वेदी"},"2":{"en":"Francis Kulandai","hi":"फ्रांसिस कुलंदई"},"3":{"en":"Pallavi Krishnan","hi":"पल्लवी कृष्णन"},"4":{"en":"R. Ravi Kannan","hi":"आर. रवि कन्नन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Pallavi Krishnan</b><br><b>Pallavi Krishnan</b> is a Mohiniyattam exponent and not a Ramon Magsaysay Award recipient, while the other three names on the list are well-known Magsaysay awardees.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Sanjiv Chaturvedi</b>, an Indian Forest Service officer, won the Magsaysay Award in 2016 for his work against corruption in the health sector.<br>• <b>Francis Kulandai</b> (a Jesuit priest known for rural uplift in Madurai) and <b>R. Ravi Kannan</b>, the surgical oncologist of Cachar Cancer Hospital, are Magsaysay awardees; Dr. Kannan received it in 2023.<br>• The Ramon Magsaysay Award, set up in 1957, is called Asia's <b>Nobel Prize</b> and is given by the Rockefeller Brothers Fund-backed Ramon Magsaysay Award Foundation in Manila.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because Pallavi Krishnan is not a recipient of the award.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – पल्लवी कृष्णन</b><br><b>पल्लवी कृष्णन (Pallavi Krishnan)</b> मोहिनीअट्टम की प्रतिपादक हैं और रेमन मैग्सेसे पुरस्कार प्राप्तकर्ता नहीं हैं, जबकि सूची में दिए अन्य तीन नाम प्रसिद्ध मैग्सेसे विजेता हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारतीय वन सेवा अधिकारी <b>संजीव चतुर्वेदी</b> ने स्वास्थ्य क्षेत्र में भ्रष्टाचार के विरुद्ध कार्य के लिए 2016 में मैग्सेसे पुरस्कार जीता।<br>• <b>फ्रांसिस कुलंदई</b> (मदुरै में ग्रामीण उत्थान के लिए प्रसिद्ध जेसुइट पादरी) तथा कछार कैंसर अस्पताल के सर्जिकल ऑन्कोलॉजिस्ट <b>आर. रवि कन्नन</b> मैग्सेसे विजेता हैं; डॉ. कन्नन को यह 2023 में मिला।<br>• 1957 में स्थापित रेमन मैग्सेसे पुरस्कार को एशिया का <b>नोबेल पुरस्कार</b> कहा जाता है और यह मनीला स्थित रेमन मैग्सेसे पुरस्कार फाउंडेशन द्वारा दिया जाता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि पल्लवी कृष्णन इस पुरस्कार की प्राप्तकर्ता नहीं हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000071714","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: India and Its Location","question":{"en":"Which of the two countries are separated by the 'Palk Strait'? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"'पाक जलडमरूमध्य' किन दो देशों को अलग करता है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"India and China","hi":"भारत तथा चीन"},"2":{"en":"India and Sri Lanka","hi":"भारत तथा श्रीलंका"},"3":{"en":"Pakistan and China","hi":"पाकिस्तान तथा चीन"},"4":{"en":"India and Nepal","hi":"भारत तथा नेपाल"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – India and Sri Lanka</b><br>The <b>Palk Strait</b> separates <b>India</b> (Tamil Nadu coast) from <b>Sri Lanka</b>, and it connects the Bay of Bengal with the Gulf of Mannar.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Palk Strait is about <b>53-80 km</b> wide, and the <b>Pamban Bridge</b> connects Rameswaram island with the mainland.<br>• <b>Adam's Bridge (Rama Setu)</b>, a chain of shoals, lies between Rameswaram and Mannar in Sri Lanka.<br>• The <b>Ten Degree Channel</b> separates the Andaman and Nicobar groups, and the <b>Nine Degree Channel</b> separates Minicoy from the main Lakshadweep group.<br>• The <b>Gulf of Mannar</b> lies south of the Palk Strait and is a Marine Biosphere Reserve.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the Palk Strait lies between India and Sri Lanka.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – भारत तथा श्रीलंका</b><br><b>पाक जलडमरूमध्य (Palk Strait)</b> <b>भारत</b> (तमिलनाडु तट) तथा <b>श्रीलंका</b> को अलग करता है और बंगाल की खाड़ी को मन्नार की खाड़ी से जोड़ता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पाक जलडमरूमध्य लगभग <b>53-80 किमी</b> चौड़ा है, तथा <b>पंबन पुल</b> रामेश्वरम द्वीप को मुख्य भूभाग से जोड़ता है।<br>• <b>एडम ब्रिज (राम सेतु)</b>, जो रेत के थोकों की श्रृंखला है, रामेश्वरम तथा श्रीलंका के मन्नार के बीच स्थित है।<br>• <b>10 डिग्री चैनल</b> अंडमान तथा निकोबार समूहों को अलग करता है, और <b>9 डिग्री चैनल</b> मिनिकॉय को लक्षद्वीप के मुख्य समूह से अलग करता है।<br>• <b>मन्नार की खाड़ी</b> पाक जलडमरूमध्य के दक्षिण में है और यह समुद्री जैवमंडल आरक्षित क्षेत्र है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि पाक जलडमरूमध्य भारत तथा श्रीलंका के बीच है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000071715","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"What natural defensive structure of Kangra Fort separates it from the Banganga and Majhi rivers? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कांगड़ा किले की कौन-सी प्राकृतिक रक्षात्मक संरचना इसे बाणगंगा तथा माझी नदियों से अलग करती है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A high wooden fence","hi":"ऊँची लकड़ी की बाड़"},"2":{"en":"A moat cut through the rocks","hi":"चट्टानों को काटकर बनी खाई"},"3":{"en":"A natural cave wall","hi":"प्राकृतिक गुफा दीवार"},"4":{"en":"A dry trench around the fort","hi":"किले के चारों ओर सूखी खाई"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – A moat cut through the rocks</b><br><b>Kangra Fort</b> in Himachal Pradesh is protected on one side by a deep <b>moat cut through the rock</b> between the fort and the <b>Banganga and Majhi</b> streams, which made direct assault very difficult.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Kangra Fort, at the confluence of the Banganga and Majhi, is one of the oldest forts in India and was held by the <b>Katoch dynasty</b>.<br>• It was captured by <b>Mahmud of Ghazni</b> in 1009, and later by Akbar's general Khawaja Abdul Rahim and finally by the Sikh commander <b>Ranjit Singh</b> in 1809.<br>• The fort suffered major damage in the <b>1905 Kangra earthquake</b>.<br>• A dry trench is not a natural structure, and the moat of Kangra was cut through hard rock, not a wooden fence or cave wall.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the rock-cut moat is the fort's natural defensive barrier.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – चट्टानों को काटकर बनी खाई</b><br>हिमाचल प्रदेश का <b>कांगड़ा किला</b> एक ओर से किले तथा <b>बाणगंगा एवं माझी</b> नदियों के बीच <b>चट्टान को काटकर बनी गहरी खाई</b> से सुरक्षित है, जिससे सीधा आक्रमण अत्यंत कठिन था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बाणगंगा तथा माझी के संगम पर स्थित कांगड़ा किला भारत के प्राचीनतम किलों में है और <b>कटोच वंश</b> के अधीन रहा।<br>• इसे 1009 में <b>महमूद गजनवी</b> ने तथा बाद में अकबर के सेनापति ख्वाजा अब्दुल रहीम ने और अंततः 1809 में सिख सेनापति <b>रंजीत सिंह</b> ने जीता।<br>• <b>1905 के कांगड़ा भूकंप</b> में किले को भारी क्षति हुई।<br>• सूखी खाई प्राकृतिक संरचना नहीं है, तथा कांगड़ा की खाई कठोर चट्टान को काटकर बनाई गई थी, लकड़ी की बाड़ या गुफा दीवार नहीं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि चट्टान-कटी खाई किले की प्राकृतिक रक्षात्मक बाधा है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000071716","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"The National Mission on Biodiversity and Human Well-Being, mentioned in the 2025 vision document, is primarily anchored by which of the following? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"2025 के विज़न दस्तावेज में उल्लिखित राष्ट्रीय जैव विविधता एवं मानव कल्याण मिशन मुख्य रूप से निम्नलिखित में से किससे संबद्ध है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"NITI Aayog and Ministry of Finance","hi":"नीति आयोग तथा वित्त मंत्रालय"},"2":{"en":"Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change and PM-STIAC","hi":"पर्यावरण, वन एवं जलवायु परिवर्तन मंत्रालय तथा PM-STIAC"},"3":{"en":"Ministry of Agriculture and ICAR","hi":"कृषि मंत्रालय तथा ICAR"},"4":{"en":"Ministry of Science & Technology and ISRO","hi":"विज्ञान एवं प्रौद्योगिकी मंत्रालय तथा ISRO"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change and PM-STIAC</b><br>The <b>National Mission on Biodiversity and Human Well-Being</b> is anchored by the <b>Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change</b> together with the <b>Prime Minister's Science, Technology and Innovation Advisory Council (PM-STIAC)</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The mission was developed by the <b>National Biodiversity Authority</b> and experts led by Prof. Kamal Bawa, and its vision document was released in 2025.<br>• Its focus areas are <b>biodiversity documentation, restoration of ecosystems, sustainable agriculture, bio-economy and biodiversity education</b>.<br>• PM-STIAC is the apex advisory body that advises the Prime Minister on science, technology and innovation missions.<br>• ICAR and the Ministry of Science &amp; Technology are partners in specific components, but the anchoring ministry is MoEFCC.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because MoEFCC and PM-STIAC anchor the mission.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पर्यावरण, वन एवं जलवायु परिवर्तन मंत्रालय तथा PM-STIAC</b><br><b>राष्ट्रीय जैव विविधता एवं मानव कल्याण मिशन (National Mission on Biodiversity and Human Well-Being)</b> <b>पर्यावरण, वन एवं जलवायु परिवर्तन मंत्रालय</b> तथा <b>प्रधानमंत्री विज्ञान, प्रौद्योगिकी एवं नवाचार सलाहकार परिषद (PM-STIAC)</b> द्वारा संचालित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह मिशन <b>राष्ट्रीय जैव विविधता प्राधिकरण</b> तथा प्रो. कमल बावा के नेतृत्व वाले विशेषज्ञों द्वारा विकसित किया गया, और इसका विज़न दस्तावेज 2025 में जारी हुआ।<br>• इसके केंद्रीय क्षेत्र <b>जैव विविधता प्रलेखन, पारिस्थितिकी तंत्र का पुनर्स्थापन, सतत कृषि, जैव-अर्थव्यवस्था तथा जैव विविधता शिक्षा</b> हैं।<br>• PM-STIAC शीर्ष सलाहकार निकाय है जो प्रधानमंत्री को विज्ञान, प्रौद्योगिकी तथा नवाचार मिशनों पर सलाह देता है।<br>• ICAR तथा विज्ञान एवं प्रौद्योगिकी मंत्रालय विशिष्ट घटकों में भागीदार हैं, परंतु संचालक मंत्रालय MoEFCC है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि मिशन का संचालन MoEFCC तथा PM-STIAC करते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000071717","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: South Indian History & Tripartite Struggle and Cholas","question":{"en":"Which fertile region received diverted river water from the \"Grand Anicut\" developed during the period of the Chola king Karikala? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"चोल राजा करिकाल के काल में विकसित \"ग्रैंड एनीकट\" से जल किस उपजाऊ क्षेत्र में मोड़ा गया? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The Kaveri delta region","hi":"कावेरी डेल्टा प्रदेश"},"2":{"en":"The Krishna delta region","hi":"कृष्णा डेल्टा प्रदेश"},"3":{"en":"The Godavari delta region","hi":"गोदावरी डेल्टा प्रदेश"},"4":{"en":"The Mahanadi delta region","hi":"महानदी डेल्टा प्रदेश"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – The Kaveri delta region</b><br>The <b>Grand Anicut (Kallanai)</b>, built on the Kaveri in the period of the Chola king <b>Karikala</b>, diverted river water to irrigate the fertile <b>Kaveri delta</b>, which became the rice granary of the Cholas.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Kallanai, near Tiruchirappalli, is regarded as one of the <b>oldest functioning water-diversion structures</b> in the world and was later extended by the British in the 19th century.<br>• Karikala is also credited with raising the banks of the Kaveri and building the Karikala Cholan Maligai.<br>• The Kaveri delta region was called <b>Cholamandalam</b>, and its fertile tracts supported the great Chola temple cities of Thanjavur and Gangaikonda Cholapuram.<br>• The Krishna, Godavari and Mahanadi deltas are in Andhra Pradesh and Odisha and were not irrigated by the Grand Anicut.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because the Grand Anicut served the Kaveri delta.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – कावेरी डेल्टा प्रदेश</b><br>चोल राजा <b>करिकाल</b> के काल में कावेरी नदी पर बना <b>ग्रैंड एनीकट (कल्लनई)</b> नदी का जल उपजाऊ <b>कावेरी डेल्टा</b> की सिंचाई हेतु मोड़ता था, जो चोलों का धान का भंडार बन गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• तिरुचिरापल्ली के निकट कल्लनई विश्व की <b>प्राचीनतम कार्यरत जल-विमोड़न संरचनाओं</b> में मानी जाती है, जिसे 19वीं सदी में ब्रिटिश शासन ने विस्तारित किया।<br>• करिकाल को कावेरी के तटों को ऊँचा करने तथा करिकाल चोलन मालिगई बनवाने का श्रेय भी दिया जाता है।<br>• कावेरी डेल्टा क्षेत्र <b>चोलमंडलम</b> कहलाता था, और इसकी उपजाऊ भूमि ने तंजावुर तथा गंगईकोंड चोलापुरम के महान चोल मंदिर नगरों को सहारा दिया।<br>• कृष्णा, गोदावरी तथा महानदी डेल्टा आंध्र प्रदेश एवं ओडिशा में हैं और ग्रैंड एनीकट से सिंचित नहीं होते।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि ग्रैंड एनीकट कावेरी डेल्टा की सेवा करता था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000071718","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Agriculture","question":{"en":"Dry farming in India is primarily practised in areas where the average annual rainfall is less than: [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में शुष्क कृषि (Dry farming) मुख्य रूप से उन क्षेत्रों में की जाती है जहाँ औसत वार्षिक वर्षा किससे कम होती है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"50 cm","hi":"50 सेमी"},"2":{"en":"80 cm","hi":"80 सेमी"},"3":{"en":"100 cm","hi":"100 सेमी"},"4":{"en":"120 cm","hi":"120 सेमी"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 80 cm</b><br><b>Dry farming</b> in India is practised where the average annual rainfall is <b>less than 80 cm</b>, mainly in Rajasthan, Gujarat, western Madhya Pradesh, parts of Maharashtra, Karnataka and Andhra Pradesh.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Dryland crops include <b>bajra, jowar, ragi, gram, groundnut</b> and other millets, which need moisture-conservation practices like contour bunding and mulching.<br>• Areas with more than 80 cm of rainfall take up <b>dryland farming</b> (rainfed) with crops such as cotton and pulses when irrigation is not available.<br>• <b>Wetland farming</b> is practised where rainfall is above 80 cm, especially in the eastern and coastal regions.<br>• The <b>ICAR's All India Coordinated Research Project for Dryland Agriculture (AICRPDA)</b> works on dry farming technology.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because dry farming is associated with rainfall of less than 80 cm.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – 80 सेमी</b><br>भारत में <b>शुष्क कृषि (Dry farming)</b> उन क्षेत्रों में की जाती है जहाँ औसत वार्षिक वर्षा <b>80 सेमी से कम</b> होती है, मुख्यतः राजस्थान, गुजरात, पश्चिमी मध्य प्रदेश, महाराष्ट्र, कर्नाटक तथा आंध्र प्रदेश के भागों में।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• शुष्क भूमि की फसलों में <b>बाजरा, ज्वार, रागी, चना, मूँगफली</b> तथा अन्य मोटे अनाज सम्मिलित हैं, जिनके लिए समोच्च बंधन तथा मल्चिंग जैसी नमी-संरक्षण विधियाँ आवश्यक हैं।<br>• 80 सेमी से अधिक वर्षा वाले क्षेत्रों में सिंचाई उपलब्ध न होने पर कपास तथा दलहन जैसी फसलों के साथ <b>वर्षा आधारित कृषि</b> होती है।<br>• <b>आर्द्रभूमि कृषि (Wetland farming)</b> वहाँ की जाती है जहाँ वर्षा 80 सेमी से अधिक हो, विशेषतः पूर्वी तथा तटीय क्षेत्रों में।<br>• <b>ICAR की शुष्क भूमि कृषि पर अखिल भारतीय समन्वित अनुसंधान परियोजना (AICRPDA)</b> शुष्क कृषि तकनीक पर कार्य करती है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि शुष्क कृषि 80 सेमी से कम वर्षा से जुड़ी है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000071719","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In Judo, what is the term for a 'full point' that ends the match immediately? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"जूडो में 'पूर्ण अंक' के लिए किस शब्द का प्रयोग होता है, जो मुकाबला तुरंत समाप्त कर देता है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Waza-ari","hi":"वाज़ा-अरी"},"2":{"en":"Yuko","hi":"युको"},"3":{"en":"Ippon","hi":"इप्पोन"},"4":{"en":"Koka","hi":"कोका"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Ippon</b><br>In Judo, an <b>Ippon</b> is the full point awarded for a clean throw, a pin of 20 seconds, a submission or disqualification, and it ends the match immediately.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Waza-ari</b> is a half point and <b>Yuko</b> (now largely merged into waza-ari scoring) is a smaller score; two waza-ari add up to an ippon.<br>• Judo was founded by <b>Jigoro Kano</b> in 1882 in Japan, and it became an Olympic sport for men in 1964 at Tokyo.<br>• The word judo means 'the gentle way', and the contest area is called the <b>tatami</b>.<br>• A judo match at the Olympics lasts <b>four minutes</b> of actual contest time.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because ippon is the full point that ends the match.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – इप्पोन</b><br>जूडो में <b>इप्पोन (Ippon)</b> पूर्ण अंक है, जो स्वच्छ थ्रो, 20 सेकंड का पिन, सबमिशन या अयोग्यता पर दिया जाता है और मुकाबला तुरंत समाप्त कर देता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>वाज़ा-अरी (Waza-ari)</b> आधा अंक है तथा <b>युको (Yuko)</b> छोटा अंक (अब मुख्यतः वाज़ा-अरी में समाहित); दो वाज़ा-अरी मिलकर इप्पोन बनते हैं।<br>• जूडो की स्थापना <b>जिगोरो कानो</b> ने 1882 में जापान में की, और यह 1964 टोक्यो में पुरुषों के लिए ओलंपिक खेल बना।<br>• जूडो का अर्थ 'कोमल मार्ग' है, तथा मुकाबले का क्षेत्र <b>तातामी (Tatami)</b> कहलाता है।<br>• ओलंपिक में जूडो का मुकाबला वास्तविक समय के <b>चार मिनट</b> का होता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि इप्पोन पूर्ण अंक है जो मुकाबला समाप्त कर देता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000071720","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Vedic Age","question":{"en":"What does the absence of the term janapada in the Rig Veda suggest? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"ऋग्वेद में 'जनपद' शब्द की अनुपस्थिति क्या दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Weak tribal ties","hi":"कमजोर जनजातीय संबंध"},"2":{"en":"Urban political control","hi":"शहरी राजनीतिक नियंत्रण"},"3":{"en":"Iron-based kingdoms","hi":"लोहा आधारित राज्य"},"4":{"en":"Lack of territorial states","hi":"क्षेत्रीय राज्यों का अभाव"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Lack of territorial states</b><br>The absence of the word <b>janapada</b> in the Rig Veda shows that early Vedic society was organised in <b>tribes (jana) and clans</b> rather than in <b>territorial states</b>, which developed only later, in the Later Vedic period.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• In the Rig Vedic period, the chief was called <b>rajan</b> and his authority depended on tribal consent and the sabha and samiti, not on territory.<br>• <b>Janapada</b> and territorial kingdoms appear in Later Vedic texts and in the age of the <b>Mahajanapadas</b> (6th century BCE).<br>• Rig Vedic economy was <b>pastoral</b>, with cattle as the chief form of wealth, so strong attachment to land came later.<br>• Weak tribal ties, urban control and iron-based kingdoms are all inappropriate inferences from an <b>absence of a term</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because the missing term points to the absence of territorial states.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – क्षेत्रीय राज्यों का अभाव</b><br>ऋग्वेद में <b>जनपद</b> शब्द की अनुपस्थिति दर्शाती है कि आरंभिक वैदिक समाज <b>जनजातियों (जन) तथा कुलों</b> में संगठित था, <b>क्षेत्रीय राज्यों</b> में नहीं; क्षेत्रीय राज्य उत्तरवर्ती वैदिक काल में विकसित हुए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ऋग्वैदिक काल में मुखिया <b>राजन</b> कहलाता था और उसकी सत्ता क्षेत्र पर नहीं, जनजातीय सहमति तथा सभा एवं समिति पर आधारित थी।<br>• <b>जनपद</b> तथा क्षेत्रीय राज्य उत्तरवैदिक ग्रंथों में तथा <b>महाजनपदों</b> (छठी शताब्दी ईसा पूर्व) के युग में दिखते हैं।<br>• ऋग्वैदिक अर्थव्यवस्था <b>पशुपालन</b> आधारित थी और गोधन संपत्ति का मुख्य रूप था, इसलिए भूमि से सुदृढ़ जुड़ाव बाद में आया।<br>• कमजोर जनजातीय संबंध, शहरी नियंत्रण तथा लोहा आधारित राज्य – ये सभी <b>शब्द की अनुपस्थिति</b> से निकले अनुचित निष्कर्ष हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि अनुपस्थित शब्द क्षेत्रीय राज्यों के अभाव की ओर संकेत करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000071721","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"In India, which position is held by Dr. V. Anantha Nageswaran, who authored and released the Economic Survey 2025-26 in early 2026? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में डॉ. वी. अनंत नागेश्वरन, जिन्होंने 2026 के आरंभ में आर्थिक समीक्षा 2025-26 लिखी तथा जारी की, किस पद पर हैं? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Finance Secretary","hi":"वित्त सचिव"},"2":{"en":"Chief Economic Adviser (CEA)","hi":"मुख्य आर्थिक सलाहकार (CEA)"},"3":{"en":"Governor of the Reserve Bank of India (RBI)","hi":"भारतीय रिज़र्व बैंक (RBI) के गवर्नर"},"4":{"en":"Chief Executive Officer of the National Institution for Transforming India (NITI Aayog)","hi":"नीति आयोग के मुख्य कार्यकारी अधिकारी"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Chief Economic Adviser (CEA)</b><br><b>Dr. V. Anantha Nageswaran</b> is the <b>Chief Economic Adviser</b> to the Government of India and, as head of the Economic Division of the Finance Ministry, authors and releases the annual <b>Economic Survey</b>, including the 2025-26 Survey.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The CEA is appointed by the <b>Appointments Committee of the Cabinet</b> for a three-year term and holds the rank of Secretary to the Government of India.<br>• Dr. Nageswaran took charge as CEA in <b>January 2022</b>, succeeding K.V. Subramanian.<br>• The <b>Economic Survey</b> is tabled in Parliament one day before the Union Budget.<br>• <b>T.V. Somanathan</b> was the Finance Secretary and later became RBI Governor; <b>Sanjay Malhotra</b> is the RBI Governor and <b>B.V.R. Subrahmanyam</b> has served as NITI Aayog CEO.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the Economic Survey is authored and released by the CEA.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – मुख्य आर्थिक सलाहकार (CEA)</b><br><b>डॉ. वी. अनंत नागेश्वरन (Dr. V. Anantha Nageswaran)</b> भारत सरकार के <b>मुख्य आर्थिक सलाहकार</b> हैं और वित्त मंत्रालय के आर्थिक प्रभाग के प्रमुख के रूप में वार्षिक <b>आर्थिक समीक्षा</b>, जिसमें 2025-26 की समीक्षा भी सम्मिलित है, लिखते एवं जारी करते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• CEA की नियुक्ति <b>मंत्रिमंडल की नियुक्ति समिति</b> द्वारा तीन वर्ष के कार्यकाल के लिए होती है और उन्हें भारत सरकार के सचिव का दर्जा प्राप्त होता है।<br>• डॉ. नागेश्वरन ने <b>जनवरी 2022</b> में के. वी. सुब्रमण्यन के स्थान पर CEA का पदभार ग्रहण किया।<br>• <b>आर्थिक समीक्षा</b> केंद्रीय बजट से एक दिन पूर्व संसद में प्रस्तुत की जाती है।<br>• <b>टी. वी. सोमनाथन</b> वित्त सचिव रहे और बाद में RBI गवर्नर बने; <b>संजय मल्होत्रा</b> RBI गवर्नर हैं तथा <b>बी. वी. आर. सुब्रह्मण्यम</b> नीति आयोग के CEO रहे हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि आर्थिक समीक्षा CEA द्वारा लिखी एवं जारी की जाती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000071722","section":"GK","topic":"Biology: Plant and Animal Kingdom","question":{"en":"Which of the following structural features serves as a defining evolutionary milestone characteristic of the division Pteridophyta? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी संरचनात्मक विशेषता टेरिडोफाइटा (Pteridophyta) विभाग की एक परिभाषित विकासवादी उपलब्धि है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Presence of true flowers","hi":"वास्तविक पुष्पों की उपस्थिति"},"2":{"en":"Presence of vascular tissues","hi":"संवहनी ऊतकों (Vascular tissues) की उपस्थिति"},"3":{"en":"Absence of true roots","hi":"वास्तविक जड़ों का अभाव"},"4":{"en":"Development of naked ovules","hi":"नग्न बीजांडों का विकास"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Presence of vascular tissues</b><br><b>Pteridophytes</b> are the first land plants with a true <b>vascular system (xylem and phloem)</b>, which is their defining evolutionary advance over bryophytes and gives them the name 'vascular cryptogams'.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Pteridophytes have well-developed <b>roots, stems and leaves</b> with vascular tissue, but they reproduce by <b>spores</b> and do not form seeds or flowers.<br>• Their life cycle shows a dominant <b>sporophyte</b> and a small independent gametophyte (prothallus).<br>• <b>True flowers</b> and <b>naked ovules</b> appear only in angiosperms and gymnosperms respectively, which are more advanced.<br>• Bryophytes, not pteridophytes, are the group with <b>no true roots</b> and no vascular tissue.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because vascular tissue is the key milestone of Pteridophyta.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – संवहनी ऊतकों (Vascular tissues) की उपस्थिति</b><br><b>टेरिडोफाइटा (Pteridophytes)</b> वे प्रथम स्थल पादप हैं जिनमें वास्तविक <b>संवहनी तंत्र (जाइलम तथा फ्लोएम)</b> होता है; यही उनकी ब्रायोफाइटा से मुख्य विकासवादी विशेषता है और इसी कारण उन्हें 'संवहनी क्रिप्टोगैम' कहा जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• टेरिडोफाइटा में संवहनी ऊतक के साथ सुविकसित <b>जड़, तना तथा पत्तियाँ</b> होती हैं, परंतु इनमें <b>बीजाणुओं</b> द्वारा प्रजनन होता है और बीज एवं पुष्प नहीं बनते।<br>• इनके जीवन चक्र में <b>स्पोरोफाइट</b> प्रमुख तथा गैमेटोफाइट (प्रोथैलस) छोटा और स्वतंत्र होता है।<br>• <b>वास्तविक पुष्प</b> तथा <b>नग्न बीजांड</b> क्रमशः आवृतबीजी तथा अनावृतबीजी में आते हैं, जो अधिक विकसित हैं।<br>• <b>वास्तविक जड़ों का अभाव</b> तथा संवहनी ऊतक का अभाव ब्रायोफाइटा की विशेषता है, टेरिडोफाइटा की नहीं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि संवहनी ऊतक टेरिडोफाइटा की मुख्य उपलब्धि है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000071723","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"During a trial, the court concludes that a fact is so highly probable that a prudent person would act on the assumption that it exists, although there is no absolute certainty. Under the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam 2023, in India such a fact is classified as: [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"विचारण के दौरान न्यायालय यह निष्कर्ष निकालता है कि कोई तथ्य इतना अधिक संभाव्य है कि विवेकशील व्यक्ति उसके अस्तित्व को मानकर कार्य करेगा, यद्यपि पूर्ण निश्चितता नहीं है। भारत में भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम 2023 के अंतर्गत ऐसा तथ्य किस रूप में वर्गीकृत होता है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Disproved","hi":"असिद्ध (Disproved)"},"2":{"en":"Not proved","hi":"सिद्ध नहीं (Not proved)"},"3":{"en":"Proved","hi":"सिद्ध (Proved)"},"4":{"en":"Conclusive proof","hi":"निर्णायक प्रमाण (Conclusive proof)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Proved</b><br>Under Section 3 of the <b>Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, 2023</b> a fact is said to be <b>proved</b> when, after considering the matters before it, the court either believes it to exist or considers its existence so probable that a prudent man ought, under the circumstances, to act upon the supposition that it exists.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• A fact is <b>disproved</b> when the court believes it does not exist or considers its non-existence so probable that a prudent man ought to act on that supposition.<br>• A fact is <b>not proved</b> when it is neither proved nor disproved – there is doubt either way.<br>• Courts in India follow the <b>prudent man test</b>, not absolute certainty, which is why the standard is 'beyond reasonable doubt' in criminal cases.<br>• <b>Conclusive proof</b> is used for statutory irrebuttable presumptions, e.g. a child below seven years cannot commit an offence.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the described situation exactly matches the definition of 'proved'.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – सिद्ध (Proved)</b><br><b>भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 2023</b> की धारा 3 के अंतर्गत तथ्य <b>सिद्ध</b> तब माना जाता है जब न्यायालय, समक्ष उपलब्ध तथ्यों पर विचार करके, या तो उसके अस्तित्व में विश्वास करता है या उसके अस्तित्व को इतना संभाव्य मानता है कि परिस्थितियों में विवेकशील व्यक्ति उस मान्यता पर कार्य करे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• तथ्य <b>असिद्ध (Disproved)</b> तब होता है जब न्यायालय मानता है कि वह नहीं है, या उसका अभाव इतना संभाव्य है कि विवेकशील व्यक्ति उसी मान्यता पर कार्य करे।<br>• तथ्य <b>सिद्ध नहीं (Not proved)</b> तब होता है जब वह न सिद्ध है न असिद्ध – दोनों ओर संदेह है।<br>• भारत के न्यायालय <b>विवेकशील व्यक्ति परीक्षण (Prudent man test)</b> अपनाते हैं, पूर्ण निश्चितता को नहीं; इसी कारण आपराधिक मामलों में मानक 'उचित संदेह से परे' है।<br>• <b>निर्णायक प्रमाण (Conclusive proof)</b> सांविधिक अप्रतिसंहरणीय उपधारणाओं के लिए प्रयुक्त होता है, जैसे सात वर्ष से कम आयु का बालक अपराध नहीं कर सकता।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि वर्णित स्थिति 'सिद्ध' की परिभाषा से पूर्णतः मेल खाती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000071724","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Important Acts","question":{"en":"Which of the following best describes the role of the B.N. Rau Committee (1941) in Indian legal history? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय विधिक इतिहास में बी. एन. राव समिति (1941) की भूमिका का सर्वोत्तम वर्णन निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It directly drafted the Uniform Civil Code.","hi":"इसने सीधे समान नागरिक संहिता का प्रारूप तैयार किया।"},"2":{"en":"It focused exclusively on Muslim law reforms.","hi":"इसने केवल मुस्लिम विधि सुधारों पर ध्यान दिया।"},"3":{"en":"It aimed to codify Hindu law with focus on gender equality.","hi":"इसका उद्देश्य लैंगिक समानता पर ध्यान देते हुए हिंदू विधि का संहिताबद्ध करण करना था।"},"4":{"en":"It rejected all forms of codified personal laws.","hi":"इसने संहिताबद्ध व्यक्तिगत विधियों के सभी रूपों को अस्वीकार किया।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – It aimed to codify Hindu law with focus on gender equality.</b><br>The <b>B.N. Rau Committee (1941)</b> was set up by the Government of India to examine and codify <b>Hindu law</b>, and it recommended reforms with a strong emphasis on <b>gender equality</b>, particularly on a woman's right to property and marriage.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Its recommendations led to the <b>Hindu Code Bill</b>, moved in Parliament by Dr. B.R. Ambedkar, which was later split into the <b>Hindu Marriage Act 1955, Hindu Succession Act 1956, Hindu Minority and Guardianship Act 1956</b> and <b>Hindu Adoptions and Maintenance Act 1956</b>.<br>• The Committee was chaired by <b>B.N. Rau</b>, who later became the Constitutional Adviser who prepared the first draft of the Indian Constitution.<br>• It did not draft the Uniform Civil Code and did not deal solely with Muslim law.<br>• The Hindu Succession (Amendment) Act, 2005 finally made daughters <b>coparceners</b> by birth, realising the Committee's vision of gender equality.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the Committee aimed to codify Hindu law with a focus on gender equality.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – इसका उद्देश्य लैंगिक समानता पर ध्यान देते हुए हिंदू विधि का संहिताबद्ध करण करना था।</b><br><b>बी. एन. राव समिति (1941)</b> को भारत सरकार ने <b>हिंदू विधि</b> की जाँच तथा संहिताबद्ध करण के लिए गठित किया था, और इसने <b>लैंगिक समानता</b> पर, विशेषतः महिला के संपत्ति तथा विवाह संबंधी अधिकार पर, बल देते हुए सुधारों की सिफारिश की।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसकी सिफारिशों से <b>हिंदू कोड बिल</b> बना, जिसे डॉ. बी. आर. अंबेडकर ने संसद में प्रस्तुत किया; बाद में यह <b>हिंदू विवाह अधिनियम 1955, हिंदू उत्तराधिकार अधिनियम 1956, हिंदू अल्पवयस्कता एवं संरक्षकता अधिनियम 1956</b> तथा <b>हिंदू दत्तक एवं भरण-पोषण अधिनियम 1956</b> में विभाजित हुआ।<br>• समिति के अध्यक्ष <b>बी. एन. राव</b> थे, जो बाद में संविधान सभा के संवैधानिक सलाहकार बने और जिन्होंने भारतीय संविधान का प्रथम प्रारूप तैयार किया।<br>• इसने समान नागरिक संहिता का प्रारूप नहीं बनाया तथा केवल मुस्लिम विधि पर कार्य नहीं किया।<br>• <b>हिंदू उत्तराधिकार (संशोधन) अधिनियम, 2005</b> ने अंततः पुत्रियों को जन्म से <b>सहदायिक (Coparcener)</b> बनाकर समिति की लैंगिक समानता की दृष्टि को साकार किया।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि समिति का उद्देश्य लैंगिक समानता पर ध्यान देते हुए हिंदू विधि का संहिताबद्ध करण था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000071725","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: Delhi Sultanate","question":{"en":"Consider the following statements regarding the Indo-Islamic architecture of Gujarat:<br>1. This architectural style incorporated decorative elements from regional Hindu temple traditions.<br>2. The bell-and-chain motif was commonly used in the construction of its structures.<br>Which of the statements given above is/are <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"गुजरात की इंडो-इस्लामिक स्थापत्य कला के संबंध में निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार करें:<br>1. इस स्थापत्य शैली ने क्षेत्रीय हिंदू मंदिर परंपराओं से अलंकरणात्मक तत्वों को समाहित किया।<br>2. इसकी संरचनाओं के निर्माण में घंटी-श्रृंखला (bell-and-chain) अलंकरण सामान्यतः प्रयुक्त होता था।<br>उपर्युक्त कथनों में से कौन-सा/से <b>सही</b> है/हैं? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 only","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"2 only","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2","hi":"1 और 2 दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2","hi":"न 1 न 2"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Both 1 and 2</b><br>Gujarat's Indo-Islamic architecture, best seen in the mosques and tombs of <b>Ahmedabad</b>, freely borrowed <b>decorative motifs from regional Hindu and Jain temple traditions</b>, and the <b>bell-and-chain motif</b> was one of the most commonly used ornaments on its minarets, arches and walls.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The finest examples are the <b>Jama Masjid of Ahmedabad (1424)</b>, the <b>Sidi Saiyyed Mosque</b> (famous for its stone lattice 'jali' work) and the <b>Rani ka Hazira</b>.<br>• Sultanate buildings in Gujarat used <b>reused temple pillars, corbelled brackets, toranas and lotus motifs</b>, showing a true synthesis of styles.<br>• The <b>bell-and-chain</b> ornament, originally a Hindu temple motif, became a standard decorative device in Gujarati mosques and tombs.<br>• This fusion is called the <b>provincial Indo-Islamic style</b>, distinct from the imperial Mughal style.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because both statements about Gujarat's Indo-Islamic architecture are correct.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 1 और 2 दोनों</b><br>गुजरात की इंडो-इस्लामिक स्थापत्य कला, जो <b>अहमदाबाद</b> की मस्जिदों तथा मकबरों में सर्वोत्तम दिखती है, ने <b>क्षेत्रीय हिंदू एवं जैन मंदिर परंपराओं से अलंकरणात्मक तत्व</b> उदारतापूर्वक ग्रहण किए, तथा <b>घंटी-श्रृंखला (Bell-and-chain) अलंकरण</b> उसके मीनारों, मेहराबों एवं दीवारों पर सर्वाधिक प्रयुक्त अलंकरणों में एक था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसके श्रेष्ठ उदाहरण <b>अहमदाबाद की जामा मस्जिद (1424)</b>, <b>सिदी सैय्यद मस्जिद</b> (अपने पत्थर की जाली के काम के लिए प्रसिद्ध) तथा <b>रानी का हजीरा</b> हैं।<br>• गुजरात की सल्तनतकालीन इमारतों में <b>पुनः प्रयुक्त मंदिर स्तंभ, कॉर्बल ब्रैकेट, तोरण तथा कमल अलंकरण</b> प्रयुक्त हुए, जो शैलियों का वास्तविक समन्वय दर्शाते हैं।<br>• मूलतः हिंदू मंदिर का अलंकरण रहा <b>घंटी-श्रृंखला</b> गुजरात की मस्जिदों एवं मकबरों में मानक अलंकरण बन गया।<br>• इस समन्वय को <b>प्रांतीय इंडो-इस्लामिक शैली</b> कहा जाता है, जो शाही मुगल शैली से भिन्न है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि गुजरात की इंडो-इस्लामिक स्थापत्य कला के दोनों कथन सही हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000071726","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: National Parks","question":{"en":"The Chhari-Dhand Wetland, announced as a new addition to India's Ramsar network in 2026, is situated in which of the following states? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"2026 में भारत के रामसर नेटवर्क में नवीनतम जुड़ाव के रूप में घोषित छरी-धांद आर्द्रभूमि निम्नलिखित में से किस राज्य में स्थित है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Bihar","hi":"बिहार"},"2":{"en":"Uttar Pradesh","hi":"उत्तर प्रदेश"},"3":{"en":"Gujarat","hi":"गुजरात"},"4":{"en":"Rajasthan","hi":"राजस्थान"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Gujarat</b><br><b>Chhari-Dhand</b>, a seasonal wetland in the Banni grassland of <b>Kutch district, Gujarat</b>, was announced as a new Ramsar site, adding to India's Ramsar network in 2026.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Chhari-Dhand is a <b>saline wetland</b> in the Banni grassland and is an important stopover for migratory birds such as the demoiselle crane and the houbara bustard.<br>• Gujarat already has Ramsar sites like <b>Nalsarovar, Thol, Wadhwana, Khijadiya</b> and the Gulf of Kutch marine area.<br>• Ramsar sites are wetlands of international importance designated under the <b>Ramsar Convention, 1971</b>, signed in Iran; India became a party in 1982.<br>• India's first Ramsar sites were <b>Chilika Lake (Odisha) and Keoladeo Ghana (Rajasthan)</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because Chhari-Dhand wetland is situated in Gujarat.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – गुजरात</b><br><b>छरी-धांद (Chhari-Dhand)</b>, जो <b>गुजरात के कच्छ जिले</b> के बन्नी घास मैदान में स्थित मौसमी आर्द्रभूमि है, को 2026 में भारत के रामसर नेटवर्क में नए रामसर स्थल के रूप में घोषित किया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• छरी-धांद बन्नी घास मैदान की <b>लवणीय आर्द्रभूमि</b> है और डेमोइज़ेल क्रेन तथा हुबारा बस्टर्ड जैसे प्रवासी पक्षियों के लिए महत्वपूर्ण पड़ाव है।<br>• गुजरात में पहले से <b>नलसरोवर, थोल, वाधवाना, खिजड़िया</b> तथा कच्छ की खाड़ी का समुद्री क्षेत्र रामसर स्थल हैं।<br>• रामसर स्थल <b>रामसर कन्वेंशन, 1971</b> के अंतर्गत अंतर्राष्ट्रीय महत्व की आर्द्रभूमियाँ हैं, जो ईरान में हस्ताक्षरित हुआ; भारत 1982 में पक्षकार बना।<br>• भारत के प्रथम रामसर स्थल <b>चिल्का झील (ओडिशा) तथा केवलादेव घना (राजस्थान)</b> थे।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि छरी-धांद आर्द्रभूमि गुजरात में स्थित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000071727","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"What is the primary objective of smart mobility initiatives in smart cities? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"स्मार्ट सिटी में स्मार्ट मोबिलिटी पहलों का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Increase road congestion and travel delays","hi":"सड़क भीड़ तथा यात्रा विलंब बढ़ाना"},"2":{"en":"Improve the efficiency and safety of urban transport","hi":"शहरी परिवहन की दक्षता एवं सुरक्षा में सुधार करना"},"3":{"en":"Reduce public transport usage and accessibility","hi":"सार्वजनिक परिवहन के उपयोग तथा पहुँच को घटाना"},"4":{"en":"Promote private vehicles and discourage shared mobility","hi":"निजी वाहनों को बढ़ावा देना तथा साझा आवागमन को हतोत्साहित करना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Improve the efficiency and safety of urban transport</b><br>Smart mobility initiatives in smart cities aim to make urban transport <b>more efficient, safer and integrated</b> through intelligent traffic management, real-time information, better public transport and last-mile connectivity.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Smart Cities Mission was launched on <b>25 June 2015</b> to develop 100 smart cities with area-based development and pan-city ICT solutions.<br>• Key smart mobility components include <b>adaptive traffic signals, Integrated Command and Control Centres, smart parking, e-vehicles and cycle tracks</b>.<br>• The objective is to <b>reduce congestion, pollution and travel time</b>, not to increase them.<br>• Smart mobility promotes <b>public and shared transport</b> and discourages dependence on private vehicles.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the aim is efficient and safe urban transport.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – शहरी परिवहन की दक्षता एवं सुरक्षा में सुधार करना</b><br>स्मार्ट सिटी की स्मार्ट मोबिलिटी पहलें बुद्धिमान यातायात प्रबंधन, वास्तविक समय सूचना, बेहतर सार्वजनिक परिवहन तथा अंतिम-मील कनेक्टिविटी के माध्यम से शहरी परिवहन को <b>अधिक दक्ष, सुरक्षित एवं समन्वित</b> बनाना चाहती हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• स्मार्ट सिटी मिशन <b>25 जून 2015</b> को 100 स्मार्ट शहरों के विकास हेतु शुरू किया गया, जिसमें क्षेत्र-आधारित विकास तथा पूरे शहर में ICT समाधान सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• प्रमुख स्मार्ट मोबिलिटी घटकों में <b>अनुकूली यातायात सिग्नल, एकीकृत कमांड एवं कंट्रोल सेंटर, स्मार्ट पार्किंग, ई-वाहन तथा साइकिल ट्रैक</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• उद्देश्य <b>भीड़, प्रदूषण तथा यात्रा समय घटाना</b> है, बढ़ाना नहीं।<br>• स्मार्ट मोबिलिटी <b>सार्वजनिक एवं साझा परिवहन</b> को बढ़ावा देती है और निजी वाहनों पर निर्भरता घटाती है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि उद्देश्य दक्ष एवं सुरक्षित शहरी परिवहन है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000071728","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Which of the following economic approaches best reflects the principle of 'minimum government, maximum governance'? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी आर्थिक दृष्टिकोण 'न्यूनतम सरकार, अधिकतम शासन' के सिद्धांत को सर्वोत्तम रूप से दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Economic import substitution","hi":"आर्थिक आयात प्रतिस्थापन"},"2":{"en":"Extensive licensing","hi":"व्यापक लाइसेंसिंग"},"3":{"en":"State monopoly","hi":"राज्य एकाधिकार"},"4":{"en":"Economic liberalisation","hi":"आर्थिक उदारीकरण"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Economic liberalisation</b><br><b>Economic liberalisation</b> – reducing licences, controls and state monopoly and allowing market forces to operate – reflects the principle of <b>'minimum government, maximum governance'</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The phrase is associated with the reforms after <b>1991</b>, when the Licence Raj was dismantled through the New Industrial Policy of 1991.<br>• Liberalisation involved <b>de-licensing of industries, removal of MRTP restrictions, opening to FDI and tariff reduction</b>.<br>• <b>Import substitution, extensive licensing and state monopoly</b> all increase government control, the opposite of the stated principle.<br>• Prime Minister Narendra Modi has used the phrase to describe governance reform that reduces the state's role in everyday decisions.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because economic liberalisation best reflects minimum government and maximum governance.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – आर्थिक उदारीकरण</b><br><b>आर्थिक उदारीकरण (Economic liberalisation)</b> – लाइसेंस, नियंत्रण तथा राज्य एकाधिकार घटाकर बाजार शक्तियों को कार्य करने देना – <b>'न्यूनतम सरकार, अधिकतम शासन'</b> के सिद्धांत को दर्शाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह वाक्यांश <b>1991</b> के बाद के सुधारों से जुड़ा है, जब नई औद्योगिक नीति 1991 के माध्यम से लाइसेंस राज समाप्त किया गया।<br>• उदारीकरण में <b>उद्योगों का डी-लाइसेंसिंग, MRTP प्रतिबंधों का हटाना, FDI के लिए खोलना तथा सीमा शुल्क में कमी</b> सम्मिलित थी।<br>• <b>आयात प्रतिस्थापन, व्यापक लाइसेंसिंग तथा राज्य एकाधिकार</b> सभी सरकारी नियंत्रण बढ़ाते हैं, जो कथित सिद्धांत के विपरीत है।<br>• प्रधानमंत्री नरेंद्र मोदी ने इस वाक्यांश का प्रयोग उस शासन सुधार के लिए किया है जो दैनिक निर्णयों में राज्य की भूमिका घटाता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि आर्थिक उदारीकरण न्यूनतम सरकार तथा अधिकतम शासन को सर्वोत्तम रूप से दर्शाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000071729","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Reports and Indices","question":{"en":"The Human Development Index (HDI) primarily encourages public debate about which of the following? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मानव विकास सूचकांक (HDI) मुख्य रूप से निम्नलिखित में से किस पर सार्वजनिक बहस को प्रोत्साहित करता है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Government taxation priorities","hi":"सरकार की कराधान प्राथमिकताएँ"},"2":{"en":"Government development priorities","hi":"सरकार की विकास प्राथमिकताएँ"},"3":{"en":"Government electoral priorities","hi":"सरकार की चुनावी प्राथमिकताएँ"},"4":{"en":"Government defence priorities","hi":"सरकार की रक्षा प्राथमिकताएँ"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Government development priorities</b><br>The <b>Human Development Index</b> shifts the measure of progress from income to people's well-being and therefore encourages public debate on whether <b>government development priorities</b> are genuinely improving health, education and living standards.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• HDI is published annually in the <b>Human Development Report</b> by the <b>UNDP</b>, prepared under Mahbub ul Haq and Amartya Sen's approach.<br>• HDI has three dimensions – <b>life expectancy (health), mean and expected years of schooling (education)</b> and <b>GNI per capita (standard of living)</b>.<br>• India's HDI rank in the latest reports has been in the <b>130-135 range</b>, in the medium human development category.<br>• Taxation, electoral and defence priorities are not the dimensions the HDI measures.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the HDI is designed to question government development priorities.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सरकार की विकास प्राथमिकताएँ</b><br><b>मानव विकास सूचकांक (HDI)</b> प्रगति का माप आय से हटाकर लोगों के कल्याण पर ले जाता है, इसलिए यह इस सार्वजनिक बहस को प्रोत्साहित करता है कि <b>सरकार की विकास प्राथमिकताएँ</b> स्वास्थ्य, शिक्षा तथा जीवन-स्तर में वास्तविक सुधार कर रही हैं या नहीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• HDI <b>UNDP</b> द्वारा <b>मानव विकास प्रतिवेदन</b> में प्रतिवर्ष प्रकाशित होता है, जो महबूब-उल-हक तथा अमर्त्य सेन की दृष्टि पर आधारित है।<br>• HDI के तीन आयाम हैं – <b>जीवन प्रत्याशा (स्वास्थ्य), औसत तथा अपेक्षित विद्यालयी वर्ष (शिक्षा)</b> एवं <b>प्रति व्यक्ति GNI (जीवन-स्तर)</b>।<br>• नवीनतम प्रतिवेदनों में भारत का HDI रैंक <b>130-135 के दायरे</b> में, मध्यम मानव विकास श्रेणी में रहा है।<br>• कराधान, चुनावी तथा रक्षा प्राथमिकताएँ HDI के मापे जाने वाले आयाम नहीं हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि HDI सरकार की विकास प्राथमिकताओं पर प्रश्न उठाने के लिए बनाया गया है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000071730","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Post-Gupta Dynasties","question":{"en":"Under what unusual circumstances did Gopala establish the Pala dynasty? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"गोपाल ने किन असामान्य परिस्थितियों में पाल वंश की स्थापना की? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"He was selected by regional chiefs to restore political order in Bengal.","hi":"बंगाल में राजनीतिक व्यवस्था बहाल करने के लिए उन्हें क्षेत्रीय सरदारों ने चुना।"},"2":{"en":"He was chosen by hereditary nobles to succeed the last ruler of Bengal.","hi":"बंगाल के अंतिम शासक के उत्तराधिकारी के रूप में उन्हें वंशानुगत सरदारों ने चुना।"},"3":{"en":"He was proclaimed by military commanders after defeating a rival kingdom.","hi":"एक प्रतिद्वंद्वी राज्य को पराजित करने के बाद सैन्य कमांडरों ने उन्हें घोषित किया।"},"4":{"en":"He was nominated by religious leaders to establish their authority in Bengal.","hi":"बंगाल में अपना प्रभुत्व स्थापित करने के लिए धार्मिक नेताओं ने उन्हें नामित किया।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – He was selected by regional chiefs to restore political order in Bengal.</b><br>After the death of Shashanka and the period of Matsyanyaya (lawlessness) in Bengal, the regional chiefs <b>elected Gopala</b> to restore political order, and he founded the <b>Pala dynasty</b> around 750 CE.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Pala dynasty ruled Bengal and Bihar from the 8th to the 12th century, with capitals at <b>Gauda and Vikramashila/Pataliputra</b>.<br>• Gopala was succeeded by <b>Dharmapala</b> and <b>Devapala</b>, under whom the Pala empire reached its height.<br>• The Palas were great patrons of <b>Mahayana Buddhism</b> and founded the monasteries of <b>Vikramashila, Somapura (Paharpur) and Odantapuri</b>.<br>• The election of Gopala is often described as the first evidence of a <b>muted elective principle</b> in early medieval Indian polity.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because Gopala was chosen by regional chiefs to end anarchy in Bengal.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – बंगाल में राजनीतिक व्यवस्था बहाल करने के लिए उन्हें क्षेत्रीय सरदारों ने चुना।</b><br>शशांक की मृत्यु तथा बंगाल में मात्स्यन्याय (अराजकता) के काल के बाद क्षेत्रीय सरदारों ने <b>गोपाल का निर्वाचन</b> राजनीतिक व्यवस्था बहाल करने के लिए किया, और उन्होंने लगभग 750 ईस्वी में <b>पाल वंश</b> की स्थापना की।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पाल वंश ने 8वीं से 12वीं शताब्दी तक बंगाल तथा बिहार पर शासन किया, जिनकी राजधानियाँ <b>गौड़ तथा विक्रमशिला/पाटलिपुत्र</b> थीं।<br>• गोपाल के बाद <b>धर्मपाल</b> तथा <b>देवपाल</b> शासक बने, जिनके अंतर्गत पाल साम्राज्य अपने शिखर पर पहुँचा।<br>• पाल <b>महायान बौद्ध धर्म</b> के महान संरक्षक थे और उन्होंने <b>विक्रमशिला, सोमपुर (पहाड़पुर) तथा ओदंतपुरी</b> के विहारों की स्थापना की।<br>• गोपाल के निर्वाचन को प्रारंभिक मध्यकालीन भारतीय राजनीति में <b>निर्वाचन सिद्धांत के प्रथम प्रमाण</b> के रूप में वर्णित किया जाता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि बंगाल की अराजकता समाप्त करने के लिए क्षेत्रीय सरदारों ने गोपाल को चुना था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000071731","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Examine the frequency polygon below to answer the following question.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q51.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>What is the total number of participants?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q51.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई आवृत्ति बहुभुज का अध्ययन करके निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q51.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>प्रतिभागियों की कुल संख्या क्या है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q51.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"75"},"2":{"en":"85"},"3":{"en":"90"},"4":{"en":"73"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"From the polygon, the number of participants in each age group is:<br>20–30 → 15, 30–40 → 25, 40–50 → 20, 50–60 → 10, 60–70 → 5, 70–80 → 0<br>Total = \\(15 + 25 + 20 + 10 + 5 + 0 = \\boxed{75}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 75.</b>","hi":"बहुभुज से प्रत्येक आयु वर्ग में प्रतिभागियों की संख्या:<br>20–30 → 15, 30–40 → 25, 40–50 → 20, 50–60 → 10, 60–70 → 5, 70–80 → 0<br>कुल = \\(15 + 25 + 20 + 10 + 5 + 0 = \\boxed{75}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 75 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q51.jpg"]}},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000071732","section":"MATH","topic":"Partnership","question":{"en":"A and B invested in a business in the ratio 3:2. If 5% of total profit is donated to a relief fund and A's share of profit is ₹4,275, find the total profit. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"A और B ने एक व्यवसाय में 3:2 के अनुपात में निवेश किया। यदि कुल लाभ का 5% राहत कोष में दान किया जाता है और A का लाभांश ₹4,275 है, तो कुल लाभ ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹7,000"},"2":{"en":"₹7,500"},"3":{"en":"₹8,200"},"4":{"en":"₹8,000"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let the total profit be \\(P\\) and the distributable profit be \\(0.95P\\).<br>A's share = \\(\\frac{3}{5} \\times 0.95P = 0.57P\\)<br>\\(0.57P = 4275 \\Rightarrow P = \\frac{4275}{0.57}\\)<br>\\(P = \\boxed{7500}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹7,500.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए कुल लाभ \\(P\\) है और वितरण योग्य लाभ \\(0.95P\\) है।<br>A का हिस्सा = \\(\\frac{3}{5} \\times 0.95P = 0.57P\\)<br>\\(0.57P = 4275 \\Rightarrow P = \\frac{4275}{0.57}\\)<br>\\(P = \\boxed{7500}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹7,500 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000071733","section":"MATH","topic":"Time Speed and Distance","question":{"en":"A plane travels from point A to point B in 21 hours. If the plane's speed decreases by 220 km/h, the travel time for the same distance increases to 26 hours. What is the total distance between A and B in kilometers? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक विमान बिंदु A से बिंदु B तक 21 घंटे में पहुँचता है। यदि विमान की चाल 220 km/h कम कर दी जाए, तो उसी दूरी के लिए यात्रा का समय बढ़कर 26 घंटे हो जाता है। A और B के बीच की कुल दूरी किलोमीटर में क्या है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"23624 km"},"2":{"en":"20540 km"},"3":{"en":"24024 km"},"4":{"en":"20800 km"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Distance is the same in both cases. Let the original speed be \\(s\\).<br>\\(21s = 26(s - 220)\\)<br>\\(26s - 21s = 26 \\times 220 \\Rightarrow 5s = 5720 \\Rightarrow s = 1144\\) km/h<br>Distance = \\(21 \\times 1144 = \\boxed{24024}\\) km<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 24024 km.</b>","hi":"दोनों स्थितियों में दूरी समान है। मान लीजिए मूल चाल \\(s\\) है।<br>\\(21s = 26(s - 220)\\)<br>\\(26s - 21s = 26 \\times 220 \\Rightarrow 5s = 5720 \\Rightarrow s = 1144\\) km/h<br>दूरी = \\(21 \\times 1144 = \\boxed{24024}\\) km<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 24024 km है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000071734","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"The area of a regular hexagon is made of how many equilateral triangles? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक समषट्भुज का क्षेत्रफल कितने समबाहु त्रिभुजों से बनता है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"222\" height=\"199\" viewBox=\"0 0 222 199\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M196 100L154 26L69 26L26 100L68 173L154 173ZM111 100L196 100M111 100L154 26M111 100L69 26M111 100L26 100M111 100L68 173M111 100L154 173\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/></svg><br>A regular hexagon can be divided by its three long diagonals into triangles with a common vertex at the centre.<br>Each triangle has two sides equal to the radius and an included angle of \\(60^\\circ\\), so each is equilateral.<br>Number of such triangles = \\(\\boxed{6}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 6.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"222\" height=\"199\" viewBox=\"0 0 222 199\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M196 100L154 26L69 26L26 100L68 173L154 173ZM111 100L196 100M111 100L154 26M111 100L69 26M111 100L26 100M111 100L68 173M111 100L154 173\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/></svg><br>एक समषट्भुज को उसके तीनों लंबे विकर्णों द्वारा केंद्र पर शीर्ष वाले त्रिभुजों में बाँटा जा सकता है।<br>प्रत्येक त्रिभुज की दो भुजाएँ त्रिज्या के बराबर हैं और उनके बीच का कोण \\(60^\\circ\\) है, अतः प्रत्येक समबाहु त्रिभुज है।<br>ऐसे त्रिभुजों की संख्या = \\(\\boxed{6}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 6 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000071735","section":"MATH","topic":"Average","question":{"en":"The average of 20 numbers was calculated as 35. It was later discovered that a number 85 was misread as 45. What is the correct average? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"20 संख्याओं का औसत 35 निकाला गया। बाद में पता चला कि संख्या 85 को गलती से 45 पढ़ा गया था। सही औसत क्या है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"54"},"2":{"en":"37"},"3":{"en":"24"},"4":{"en":"47"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Sum calculated = \\(20 \\times 35 = 700\\)<br>Correct sum = \\(700 + (85 - 45) = 740\\)<br>Correct average = \\(\\frac{740}{20} = \\boxed{37}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 37.</b>","hi":"निकाला गया योग = \\(20 \\times 35 = 700\\)<br>सही योग = \\(700 + (85 - 45) = 740\\)<br>सही औसत = \\(\\frac{740}{20} = \\boxed{37}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 37 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000071736","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"A trader sells a cabinet at a profit of 15%. If he had purchased it for 20% less and sold it for ₹40 less, he would have gained 30%. Calculate the approximate cost price. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक व्यापारी एक कैबिनेट को 15% लाभ पर बेचता है। यदि उसने इसे 20% कम पर खरीदा होता और ₹40 कम पर बेचा होता, तो उसे 30% लाभ होता। लगभग लागत मूल्य ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹545"},"2":{"en":"₹364"},"3":{"en":"₹234"},"4":{"en":"₹654"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let CP = \\(x\\).<br>Actual SP = \\(1.15x\\)<br>New CP = \\(0.8x\\), new SP = \\(1.15x - 40\\), and this gives 30% gain:<br>\\(1.15x - 40 = 1.3 \\times 0.8x = 1.04x\\)<br>\\(0.11x = 40 \\Rightarrow x = 363.6 \\approx \\boxed{364}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹364.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए लागत मूल्य = \\(x\\)<br>वास्तविक विक्रय मूल्य = \\(1.15x\\)<br>नया लागत मूल्य = \\(0.8x\\), नया विक्रय मूल्य = \\(1.15x - 40\\), जिससे 30% लाभ होता है:<br>\\(1.15x - 40 = 1.3 \\times 0.8x = 1.04x\\)<br>\\(0.11x = 40 \\Rightarrow x = 363.6 \\approx \\boxed{364}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹364 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000071737","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In ΔPBC, ∠P = 66° and ∠B = 50°. If the bisectors of ∠B and ∠C meet at T, then find the value of ∠BTC − ∠TCP? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"ΔPBC में, ∠P = 66° और ∠B = 50° है। यदि ∠B और ∠C के समद्विभाजक T पर मिलते हैं, तो ∠BTC − ∠TCP का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"83°"},"2":{"en":"76°"},"3":{"en":"97°"},"4":{"en":"91°"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"282\" height=\"208\" viewBox=\"0 0 282 208\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M90 26L26 182L256 182ZM26 182L111 124L256 182M84 39A14 14 0 0 0 100 36M48 182A22 22 0 0 0 34 161\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"124\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"86\" y=\"17\">P</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"192\">B</text><text x=\"271\" y=\"191\">C</text><text x=\"117\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"start\">T</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"11\">66°</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"167\" font-size=\"11\">50°</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\angle C = 180^\\circ - 66^\\circ - 50^\\circ = 64^\\circ\\)<br>For the triangle formed by two angle bisectors, \\(\\angle BTC = 90^\\circ + \\frac{\\angle P}{2} = 90^\\circ + 33^\\circ = 123^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\angle TCP = \\frac{\\angle C}{2} = \\frac{64^\\circ}{2} = 32^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\angle BTC - \\angle TCP = 123^\\circ - 32^\\circ = \\boxed{91^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 91°.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"282\" height=\"208\" viewBox=\"0 0 282 208\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M90 26L26 182L256 182ZM26 182L111 124L256 182M84 39A14 14 0 0 0 100 36M48 182A22 22 0 0 0 34 161\"/><circle cx=\"111\" cy=\"124\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"86\" y=\"17\">P</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"192\">B</text><text x=\"271\" y=\"191\">C</text><text x=\"117\" y=\"122\" text-anchor=\"start\">T</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"11\">66°</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"167\" font-size=\"11\">50°</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\angle C = 180^\\circ - 66^\\circ - 50^\\circ = 64^\\circ\\)<br>दो कोण समद्विभाजकों से बने त्रिभुज के लिए, \\(\\angle BTC = 90^\\circ + \\frac{\\angle P}{2} = 90^\\circ + 33^\\circ = 123^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\angle TCP = \\frac{\\angle C}{2} = \\frac{64^\\circ}{2} = 32^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\angle BTC - \\angle TCP = 123^\\circ - 32^\\circ = \\boxed{91^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 91° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000071738","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"A balloon rises vertically. From a point 50 m away, the angle of elevation changes from 30° to 60° in 10 seconds. Find the approximate height gained and vertical speed. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक गुब्बारा ऊर्ध्वाधर रूप से ऊपर उठता है। 50 m दूर एक बिंदु से, उन्नयन कोण 10 सेकंड में 30° से 60° हो जाता है। लगभग प्राप्त ऊँचाई और ऊर्ध्वाधर चाल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"49.75 m, 7.78 m/s"},"2":{"en":"47.75 m, 5.78 m/s"},"3":{"en":"57.75 m, 5.78 m/s"},"4":{"en":"50.75 m, 6.78 m/s"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"162\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 162 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 196L136 196M26 196L124 139M26 196L124 26M116 196L116 188L124 188M66 196A40 40 0 0 0 61 176M44 196A18 18 0 0 0 35 180\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M124 196L124 26\"/><circle cx=\"124\" cy=\"139\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><circle cx=\"124\" cy=\"26\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"78\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"11\">30°</text><text x=\"45\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"11\">60°</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"207\">O</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"207\">F</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"143\">B₁</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"30\">B₂</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"212\">50 m</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"87\">gain</text></g></svg><br>Initial height = \\(50\\tan 30^\\circ = \\frac{50}{\\sqrt{3}} = 28.87\\) m<br>Final height = \\(50\\tan 60^\\circ = 50\\sqrt{3} = 86.60\\) m<br>Height gained = \\(86.60 - 28.87 = 57.73 \\approx 57.75\\) m<br>Speed = \\(\\frac{57.75}{10} = 5.78\\) m/s<br>So the answer is \\(\\boxed{57.75\\ \\text{m}, 5.78\\ \\text{m/s}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 57.75 m, 5.78 m/s.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"162\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 162 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 196L136 196M26 196L124 139M26 196L124 26M116 196L116 188L124 188M66 196A40 40 0 0 0 61 176M44 196A18 18 0 0 0 35 180\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M124 196L124 26\"/><circle cx=\"124\" cy=\"139\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><circle cx=\"124\" cy=\"26\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"78\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"11\">30°</text><text x=\"45\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"11\">60°</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"207\">O</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"207\">F</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"143\">B₁</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"30\">B₂</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"212\">50 m</text><text x=\"103\" y=\"87\">gain</text></g></svg><br>प्रारंभिक ऊँचाई = \\(50\\tan 30^\\circ = \\frac{50}{\\sqrt{3}} = 28.87\\) m<br>अंतिम ऊँचाई = \\(50\\tan 60^\\circ = 50\\sqrt{3} = 86.60\\) m<br>प्राप्त ऊँचाई = \\(86.60 - 28.87 = 57.73 \\approx 57.75\\) m<br>चाल = \\(\\frac{57.75}{10} = 5.78\\) m/s<br>अतः उत्तर है \\(\\boxed{57.75\\ \\text{m}, 5.78\\ \\text{m/s}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 57.75 m, 5.78 m/s है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000071739","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A rhombus has a perimeter of 104 cm and one of its diagonals measures 48 cm. A rectangle has its sides equal to the two diagonals of this rhombus. Find the area of the rectangle (in cm²). [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक समचतुर्भुज का परिमाप 104 cm है और उसका एक विकर्ण 48 cm है। एक आयत की भुजाएँ इस समचतुर्भुज के दोनों विकर्णों के बराबर हैं। आयत का क्षेत्रफल (cm² में) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1020 cm²"},"2":{"en":"790 cm²"},"3":{"en":"960 cm²"},"4":{"en":"857 cm²"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"252\" height=\"135\" viewBox=\"0 0 252 135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 68L126 26L226 68L126 109ZM133 68L133 61L126 61\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 68L226 68M126 26L126 109\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"10\" y=\"72\">A</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"16\">B</text><text x=\"242\" y=\"72\">C</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"127\">D</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"79\">24</text><text x=\"133\" y=\"51\">x</text><text x=\"183\" y=\"33\">26 cm</text></g></svg><br>Side of the rhombus = \\(\\frac{104}{4} = 26\\) cm; half of the given diagonal = 24 cm<br>Other half diagonal = \\(\\sqrt{26^2 - 24^2} = \\sqrt{676 - 576} = 10\\) cm, so the other diagonal = 20 cm<br>Rectangle = \\(48 \\times 20 = \\boxed{960}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 960 cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"252\" height=\"135\" viewBox=\"0 0 252 135\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 68L126 26L226 68L126 109ZM133 68L133 61L126 61\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 68L226 68M126 26L126 109\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"10\" y=\"72\">A</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"16\">B</text><text x=\"242\" y=\"72\">C</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"127\">D</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"79\">24</text><text x=\"133\" y=\"51\">x</text><text x=\"183\" y=\"33\">26 cm</text></g></svg><br>समचतुर्भुज की भुजा = \\(\\frac{104}{4} = 26\\) cm; दिए गए विकर्ण का आधा = 24 cm<br>दूसरे विकर्ण का आधा = \\(\\sqrt{26^2 - 24^2} = \\sqrt{676 - 576} = 10\\) cm, अतः दूसरा विकर्ण = 20 cm<br>आयत का क्षेत्रफल = \\(48 \\times 20 = \\boxed{960}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 960 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000071740","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If cosec θ + cot θ = 3, find the value of sin θ. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि cosec θ + cot θ = 3 है, तो sin θ का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{10}{3}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{2}{5}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{3}{5}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta + \\cot\\theta = \\frac{1 + \\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta} = 3\\)<br>Also, \\(\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta - \\cot\\theta = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{1 + \\cos\\theta} = \\frac{1}{3}\\)<br>Adding: \\(2\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta = 3 + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{10}{3} \\Rightarrow \\operatorname{cosec}\\theta = \\frac{5}{3}\\)<br>\\(\\sin\\theta = \\boxed{\\frac{3}{5}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(\\frac{3}{5}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta + \\cot\\theta = \\frac{1 + \\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta} = 3\\)<br>साथ ही, \\(\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta - \\cot\\theta = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{1 + \\cos\\theta} = \\frac{1}{3}\\)<br>जोड़ने पर: \\(2\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta = 3 + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{10}{3} \\Rightarrow \\operatorname{cosec}\\theta = \\frac{5}{3}\\)<br>\\(\\sin\\theta = \\boxed{\\frac{3}{5}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(\\frac{3}{5}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000071741","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If 5 cot θ = 12, find the value of \\(\\frac{5\\cos\\theta - \\sin\\theta}{5\\cos\\theta + \\sin\\theta}\\). [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि 5 cot θ = 12 है, तो \\(\\frac{5\\cos\\theta - \\sin\\theta}{5\\cos\\theta + \\sin\\theta}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{6}{13}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{7}{13}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{11}{13}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{12}{13}\\)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(5\\cot\\theta = 12 \\Rightarrow \\cot\\theta = \\frac{12}{5}\\)<br>Divide numerator and denominator by \\(\\sin\\theta\\):<br>\\(\\frac{5\\cot\\theta - 1}{5\\cot\\theta + 1} = \\frac{12 - 1}{12 + 1} = \\boxed{\\frac{11}{13}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(\\frac{11}{13}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(5\\cot\\theta = 12 \\Rightarrow \\cot\\theta = \\frac{12}{5}\\)<br>अंश और हर दोनों को \\(\\sin\\theta\\) से भाग दीजिए:<br>\\(\\frac{5\\cot\\theta - 1}{5\\cot\\theta + 1} = \\frac{12 - 1}{12 + 1} = \\boxed{\\frac{11}{13}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(\\frac{11}{13}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000071742","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(X = \\sqrt{\\frac{4+\\sqrt{15}}{4-\\sqrt{15}}}\\), then what is the value of \\(X + \\frac{1}{X}\\)? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(X = \\sqrt{\\frac{4+\\sqrt{15}}{4-\\sqrt{15}}}\\) है, तो \\(X + \\frac{1}{X}\\) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"6"},"4":{"en":"8"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\((4 + \\sqrt{15})(4 - \\sqrt{15}) = 16 - 15 = 1\\)<br>\\(X = \\sqrt{\\frac{(4+\\sqrt{15})^2}{1}} = 4 + \\sqrt{15}\\)<br>Then \\(\\frac{1}{X} = \\frac{1}{4+\\sqrt{15}} = 4 - \\sqrt{15}\\)<br>\\(X + \\frac{1}{X} = (4 + \\sqrt{15}) + (4 - \\sqrt{15}) = \\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 8.</b>","hi":"\\((4 + \\sqrt{15})(4 - \\sqrt{15}) = 16 - 15 = 1\\)<br>\\(X = \\sqrt{\\frac{(4+\\sqrt{15})^2}{1}} = 4 + \\sqrt{15}\\)<br>तब \\(\\frac{1}{X} = \\frac{1}{4+\\sqrt{15}} = 4 - \\sqrt{15}\\)<br>\\(X + \\frac{1}{X} = (4 + \\sqrt{15}) + (4 - \\sqrt{15}) = \\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 8 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000071743","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Read the following histogram which represents the time in minutes on x-axis and number of employees on y-axis and answer the following question:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q63.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>The difference between the employees in the 9-13 and 24-31 intervals is approximate what percentage of the total number of employees?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q63.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई आवृत्ति-स्तंभ चित्र (हिस्टोग्राम) पढ़िए जिसमें x-अक्ष पर मिनटों में समय और y-अक्ष पर कर्मचारियों की संख्या दी गई है, और निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q63.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>9-13 और 24-31 अंतरालों के कर्मचारियों का अंतर कर्मचारियों की कुल संख्या का लगभग कितना प्रतिशत है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q63.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15%"},"2":{"en":"17%"},"3":{"en":"18%"},"4":{"en":"22%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"From the histogram: 8–9 → 20, 9–13 → 28, 13–18 → 15, 18–24 → 20, 24–31 → 8, 31–40 → 15, 40–50 → 14<br>Total employees = \\(20+28+15+20+8+15+14 = 120\\)<br>Difference = \\(28 - 8 = 20\\)<br>Required percentage = \\(\\frac{20}{120} \\times 100 = 16.67\\% \\approx \\boxed{17\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 17%.</b>","hi":"हिस्टोग्राम से: 8–9 → 20, 9–13 → 28, 13–18 → 15, 18–24 → 20, 24–31 → 8, 31–40 → 15, 40–50 → 14<br>कुल कर्मचारी = \\(20+28+15+20+8+15+14 = 120\\)<br>अंतर = \\(28 - 8 = 20\\)<br>अभीष्ट प्रतिशत = \\(\\frac{20}{120} \\times 100 = 16.67\\% \\approx \\boxed{17\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 17% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q63.jpg"]}},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000071744","section":"MATH","topic":"Discount","question":{"en":"An item is marked at 80% above its cost price. If it is sold at a 30% discount, what is the profit percentage? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक वस्तु का अंकित मूल्य उसके लागत मूल्य से 80% अधिक है। यदि उसे 30% छूट पर बेचा जाता है, तो लाभ प्रतिशत क्या है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"22%"},"2":{"en":"26%"},"3":{"en":"30%"},"4":{"en":"32%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let CP = 100, then MP = 180<br>SP = \\(180 \\times 0.70 = 126\\)<br>Profit = \\(126 - 100 = 26\\)<br>Profit % = \\(\\boxed{26\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 26%.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए लागत मूल्य = 100, तब अंकित मूल्य = 180<br>विक्रय मूल्य = \\(180 \\times 0.70 = 126\\)<br>लाभ = \\(126 - 100 = 26\\)<br>लाभ % = \\(\\boxed{26\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 26% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000071745","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"The following pie-chart presents the percentage distribution of different forest types within a specific geographical area. Analyse the data provided and answer the following question based on the chart.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q65.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>If the region plans to consolidate the 'Tropical Evergreen' sector, which is 30%, with the 'Scrub' sector, which is 10%, and designate all the 'Alpine' forests, which make up 15%, under the 'Deciduous' category, then what will be the percentage of the 'Deciduous' category?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q65.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिया गया पाई-चार्ट किसी विशिष्ट भौगोलिक क्षेत्र में विभिन्न वन प्रकारों के प्रतिशत वितरण को दर्शाता है। दिए गए आंकड़ों का विश्लेषण कीजिए और चार्ट के आधार पर निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q65.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>यदि क्षेत्र 'उष्णकटिबंधीय सदाबहार' (30%) को 'स्क्रब' (10%) के साथ मिलाने की योजना बनाता है, और सभी 'अल्पाइन' वनों (15%) को 'पतझड़ी' श्रेणी में रखता है, तो 'पतझड़ी' श्रेणी का प्रतिशत क्या होगा?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q65.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"35%"},"2":{"en":"40%"},"3":{"en":"45%"},"4":{"en":"50%"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"From the pie chart: Tropical Evergreen = 30%, Deciduous = 35%, Scrub = 10%, Alpine = 15%, Mangrove = 10%<br>Deciduous category after the change = existing deciduous + Alpine<br>\\(= 35\\% + 15\\% = \\boxed{50\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 50%.</b>","hi":"पाई-चार्ट से: उष्णकटिबंधीय सदाबहार = 30%, पतझड़ी = 35%, स्क्रब = 10%, अल्पाइन = 15%, मैंग्रोव = 10%<br>परिवर्तन के बाद पतझड़ी श्रेणी = वर्तमान पतझड़ी + अल्पाइन<br>\\(= 35\\% + 15\\% = \\boxed{50\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 50% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q65.jpg"]}},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000071746","section":"MATH","topic":"Partnership","question":{"en":"Three people, namely Tanistha, Lisa and Tarini start a garment business in partnership. Tanistha invests \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) of the capital for \\(\\frac{2}{5}\\) of the total time, Lisa invests \\(\\frac{2}{5}\\) of the capital for \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) of the total time and Tarini invests the rest for the entire time. If the total profit from this business is Rs. 8062, find out Lisa's share in the profit. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"तनिष्ठा, लिसा और तारिणी नामक तीन लोग साझेदारी में एक वस्त्र व्यवसाय शुरू करते हैं। तनिष्ठा कुल पूँजी का \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) भाग \\(\\frac{2}{5}\\) समय के लिए, लिसा \\(\\frac{2}{5}\\) भाग \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) समय के लिए तथा तारिणी शेष पूँजी पूरे समय के लिए निवेश करती है। यदि इस व्यवसाय से कुल लाभ Rs. 8062 है, तो लाभ में लिसा का हिस्सा ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rs. 1112"},"2":{"en":"Rs. 1390"},"3":{"en":"Rs. 1410"},"4":{"en":"Rs. 1468"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Profit shares are proportional to capital × time.<br>Tanistha = \\(\\frac{1}{5} \\times \\frac{2}{5} = \\frac{2}{25}\\), Lisa = \\(\\frac{2}{5} \\times \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{10}\\), Tarini = \\(\\frac{2}{5} \\times 1 = \\frac{2}{5}\\)<br>Multiplying by 50: Tanistha : Lisa : Tarini = 4 : 5 : 20 (total 29)<br>Lisa's share \\(= \\frac{5}{29} \\times 8062 = \\boxed{\\text{Rs. } 1390}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Rs. 1390.</b>","hi":"लाभ के हिस्से पूँजी × समय के समानुपाती होते हैं।<br>तनिष्ठा = \\(\\frac{1}{5} \\times \\frac{2}{5} = \\frac{2}{25}\\), लिसा = \\(\\frac{2}{5} \\times \\frac{1}{4} = \\frac{1}{10}\\), तारिणी = \\(\\frac{2}{5} \\times 1 = \\frac{2}{5}\\)<br>50 से गुणा करने पर: तनिष्ठा : लिसा : तारिणी = 4 : 5 : 20 (कुल 29)<br>लिसा का हिस्सा \\(= \\frac{5}{29} \\times 8062 = \\boxed{\\text{Rs. } 1390}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): Rs. 1390 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000071747","section":"MATH","topic":"Set Relation and Function","question":{"en":"If Q is dense in R and R \\ Q (the irrationals) is also dense in R, which conclusion follows directly from the density of the irrationals in R? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि Q, R में सघन है और R \\ Q (अपरिमेय संख्याएँ) भी R में सघन है, तो R में अपरिमेय संख्याओं की सघनता से सीधे कौन-सा निष्कर्ष निकलता है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Between any two irrationals there is no rational.","hi":"किन्हीं दो अपरिमेय संख्याओं के बीच कोई परिमेय संख्या नहीं होती।"},"2":{"en":"Every open interval in R contains uncountably many irrationals and countably many rational numbers.","hi":"R के प्रत्येक खुले अंतराल में अगणनीय रूप से अनेक अपरिमेय और गणनीय रूप से अनेक परिमेय संख्याएँ होती हैं।"},"3":{"en":"The closure of R \\ Q in R is R itself.","hi":"R में R \\ Q का संवृत (closure) स्वयं R है।"},"4":{"en":"Q and R \\ Q have the same cardinality.","hi":"Q और R \\ Q की गणन-संख्या (cardinality) समान है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"A set is dense in R exactly when its closure is the whole of R.<br>Since R \\ Q is given to be dense in R, its closure in R is R itself:<br>\\(\\overline{\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\mathbb{Q}} = \\mathbb{R}\\)<br>So the answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{The closure of } \\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\mathbb{Q} \\text{ in } \\mathbb{R} \\text{ is } \\mathbb{R} \\text{ itself}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): The closure of R \\ Q in R is R itself.</b>","hi":"कोई समुच्चय R में तब सघन होता है जब उसका संवृत (closure) पूरा R हो।<br>चूँकि R \\ Q को R में सघन दिया गया है, R में इसका संवृत स्वयं R है:<br>\\(\\overline{\\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\mathbb{Q}} = \\mathbb{R}\\)<br>अतः उत्तर है \\(\\boxed{\\text{R में } \\mathbb{R}\\setminus\\mathbb{Q} \\text{ का संवृत स्वयं R है}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): R में R \\ Q का संवृत (closure) स्वयं R है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000071748","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"Which of the following numbers is divisible by 11 and also a perfect square? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी संख्या 11 से विभाज्य है और पूर्ण वर्ग भी है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1936"},"2":{"en":"2025"},"3":{"en":"2401"},"4":{"en":"2809"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(1936 = 44^2\\), so it is a perfect square<br>Divisibility by 11: \\((1 + 3) - (9 + 6) = 4 - 15 = -11\\), a multiple of 11, so 1936 is divisible by 11<br>\\(\\boxed{1936}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1936.</b>","hi":"\\(1936 = 44^2\\), अतः यह पूर्ण वर्ग है<br>11 से विभाज्यता: \\((1 + 3) - (9 + 6) = 4 - 15 = -11\\), जो 11 का गुणज है, अतः 1936, 11 से विभाज्य है<br>\\(\\boxed{1936}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1936 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000071749","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"Three vessels X, Y and Z contain distinct mixtures of absolute alcohol and pure water in the ratios 3:2, 4:1 and 7:3, respectively. Pranita extracts liquid from vessels X, Y and Z in the volume ratio a:b:c and mixes them together in another vessel P. The resulting mixture in P contains alcohol and water in a 3:1 ratio. If the volume of the liquid taken out from Z is exactly 2.5 times that taken from X, determine a:b:c. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"तीन बर्तन X, Y और Z में क्रमशः 3:2, 4:1 और 7:3 के अनुपात में शुद्ध अल्कोहल और शुद्ध जल के मिश्रण हैं। प्रणिता बर्तन X, Y और Z से a:b:c आयतन अनुपात में द्रव निकालकर दूसरे बर्तन P में मिलाती है। P में प्राप्त मिश्रण में अल्कोहल और जल 3:1 के अनुपात में हैं। यदि Z से निकाला गया द्रव X से निकाले गए द्रव का ठीक 2.5 गुना है, तो a:b:c ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2:9:11"},"2":{"en":"2:11:5"},"3":{"en":"3:9:4"},"4":{"en":"3:4:7"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Alcohol fractions: X = \\(\\frac{3}{5}\\), Y = \\(\\frac{4}{5}\\), Z = \\(\\frac{7}{10}\\)<br>Given \\(c = 2.5a\\), take \\(a = 2k, c = 5k, b\\) unknown.<br>Alcohol = \\(2k \\cdot \\frac{3}{5} + b \\cdot \\frac{4}{5} + 5k \\cdot \\frac{7}{10} = 1.2k + 0.8b + 3.5k\\)<br>Water = \\(2k \\cdot \\frac{2}{5} + b \\cdot \\frac{1}{5} + 5k \\cdot \\frac{3}{10} = 0.8k + 0.2b + 1.5k\\)<br>Ratio alcohol : water = 3 : 1<br>\\(4.7k + 0.8b = 3(2.3k + 0.2b) \\Rightarrow 0.2b = 2.2k \\Rightarrow b = 11k\\)<br>\\(a : b : c = 2 : 11 : 5\\), i.e. \\(\\boxed{2:11:5}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2:11:5.</b>","hi":"अल्कोहल के भाग: X = \\(\\frac{3}{5}\\), Y = \\(\\frac{4}{5}\\), Z = \\(\\frac{7}{10}\\)<br>दिया गया है \\(c = 2.5a\\), अतः \\(a = 2k, c = 5k\\), \\(b\\) अज्ञात।<br>अल्कोहल = \\(2k \\cdot \\frac{3}{5} + b \\cdot \\frac{4}{5} + 5k \\cdot \\frac{7}{10} = 1.2k + 0.8b + 3.5k\\)<br>जल = \\(2k \\cdot \\frac{2}{5} + b \\cdot \\frac{1}{5} + 5k \\cdot \\frac{3}{10} = 0.8k + 0.2b + 1.5k\\)<br>अल्कोहल : जल = 3 : 1<br>\\(4.7k + 0.8b = 3(2.3k + 0.2b) \\Rightarrow 0.2b = 2.2k \\Rightarrow b = 11k\\)<br>\\(a : b : c = 2 : 11 : 5\\), अर्थात् \\(\\boxed{2:11:5}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 2:11:5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000071750","section":"MATH","topic":"Discount","question":{"en":"A merchant prices an item such that after offering two successive discounts of x% and 2x% on the marked price, they secure a net profit percentage equal to x% of the cost price. If the ratio of the marked price to the cost price is exactly 5 : 2, what is the value of x? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक व्यापारी किसी वस्तु का मूल्य इस प्रकार निर्धारित करता है कि अंकित मूल्य पर x% और 2x% की दो क्रमिक छूट देने के बाद उसे लागत मूल्य के x% के बराबर शुद्ध लाभ प्रतिशत प्राप्त होता है। यदि अंकित मूल्य और लागत मूल्य का अनुपात ठीक 5 : 2 है, तो x का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25%"},"2":{"en":"20%"},"3":{"en":"40%"},"4":{"en":"16%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Take CP = 2 and MP = 5. Let \\(t = \\frac{x}{100}\\).<br>SP = \\(5(1 - t)(1 - 2t)\\) and profit = \\(x\\%\\) of CP \\(= 2t\\)<br>So \\(5(1 - t)(1 - 2t) = 2 + 2t\\)<br>\\(5(1 - 3t + 2t^2) = 2 + 2t \\Rightarrow 10t^2 - 17t + 3 = 0\\)<br>\\((2t - 3)(5t - 1) = 0 \\Rightarrow t = \\frac{1}{5}\\) (the root 1.5 is rejected)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{20\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 20%.</b>","hi":"लागत मूल्य = 2 और अंकित मूल्य = 5 लीजिए। मान लीजिए \\(t = \\frac{x}{100}\\)<br>विक्रय मूल्य = \\(5(1 - t)(1 - 2t)\\) और लाभ = लागत मूल्य का \\(x\\%\\) \\(= 2t\\)<br>अतः \\(5(1 - t)(1 - 2t) = 2 + 2t\\)<br>\\(5(1 - 3t + 2t^2) = 2 + 2t \\Rightarrow 10t^2 - 17t + 3 = 0\\)<br>\\((2t - 3)(5t - 1) = 0 \\Rightarrow t = \\frac{1}{5}\\) (मूल 1.5 अस्वीकृत)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{20\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 20% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000071751","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = 11\\), where x ≠ 0, what is the value of \\(x^3 + \\frac{1}{x^3}\\)? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = 11\\) है, जहाँ x ≠ 0, तो \\(x^3 + \\frac{1}{x^3}\\) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1108"},"2":{"en":"1298"},"3":{"en":"1331"},"4":{"en":"1492"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(x^3 + \\frac{1}{x^3} = \\left(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^3 - 3\\left(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\)<br>\\(= 11^3 - 3 \\times 11 = 1331 - 33\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1298}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1298.</b>","hi":"\\(x^3 + \\frac{1}{x^3} = \\left(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^3 - 3\\left(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\)<br>\\(= 11^3 - 3 \\times 11 = 1331 - 33\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1298}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1298 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000071752","section":"MATH","topic":"Average","question":{"en":"The average of 5 consecutive multiples of 7 is 84. What is the largest multiple in this sequence? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"7 के 5 क्रमागत गुणजों का औसत 84 है। इस श्रेणी में सबसे बड़ा गुणज क्या है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"70"},"2":{"en":"91"},"3":{"en":"98"},"4":{"en":"105"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"For 5 consecutive multiples of 7, the average is the middle term.<br>Middle term = 84<br>Largest term = middle + 2 steps \\(= 84 + 2 \\times 7 = \\boxed{98}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 98.</b>","hi":"7 के 5 क्रमागत गुणजों का औसत मध्य पद होता है।<br>मध्य पद = 84<br>सबसे बड़ा पद = मध्य + 2 कदम \\(= 84 + 2 \\times 7 = \\boxed{98}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 98 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000071753","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"An automobile manufacturer tracks the production of Electric Vehicles (EVs) and Internal Combustion Engine (ICE) vehicles over three consecutive years. The relevant data is illustrated in the bar graph given below:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q73.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>What is the percentage increase in EV production from the year 2023 to 2025, and what is the percentage decrease in ICE production from the year 2023 to 2024, respectively?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q73.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक ऑटोमोबाइल निर्माता तीन क्रमागत वर्षों में इलेक्ट्रिक वाहनों (EV) और आंतरिक दहन इंजन (ICE) वाहनों के उत्पादन पर नज़र रखता है। संबंधित आंकड़े नीचे दिए गए स्तंभ ग्राफ में दर्शाए गए हैं:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q73.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>वर्ष 2023 से 2025 तक EV उत्पादन में प्रतिशत वृद्धि और वर्ष 2023 से 2024 तक ICE उत्पादन में प्रतिशत कमी क्रमशः क्या है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q73.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"180%, 25%"},"2":{"en":"75%, 25%"},"3":{"en":"75%, 12.5%"},"4":{"en":"180%, 12.5%"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"From the bar graph (units in thousands): EV → 2023: 40, 2024: 70, 2025: 112; ICE → 2023: 160, 2024: 140, 2025: 120<br>EV increase 2023 → 2025 = \\(\\frac{112 - 40}{40} \\times 100 = \\frac{72}{40} \\times 100 = 180\\%\\)<br>ICE decrease 2023 → 2024 = \\(\\frac{160 - 140}{160} \\times 100 = 12.5\\%\\)<br>So the answer is \\(\\boxed{180\\%,\\ 12.5\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 180%, 12.5%.</b>","hi":"स्तंभ ग्राफ से (इकाई हज़ार में): EV → 2023: 40, 2024: 70, 2025: 112; ICE → 2023: 160, 2024: 140, 2025: 120<br>EV में वृद्धि 2023 → 2025 = \\(\\frac{112 - 40}{40} \\times 100 = \\frac{72}{40} \\times 100 = 180\\%\\)<br>ICE में कमी 2023 → 2024 = \\(\\frac{160 - 140}{160} \\times 100 = 12.5\\%\\)<br>अतः उत्तर है \\(\\boxed{180\\%,\\ 12.5\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 180%, 12.5% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-23-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1/q73.jpg"]}},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000071754","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(a + b + c = 0\\) and \\(abc = 24\\), what is the value of \\((a + b)(b + c)(c + a)\\)? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(a + b + c = 0\\) और \\(abc = 24\\) है, तो \\((a + b)(b + c)(c + a)\\) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"−48"},"2":{"en":"−24"},"3":{"en":"24"},"4":{"en":"48"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"From \\(a + b + c = 0\\): \\(a + b = -c\\), \\(b + c = -a\\), \\(c + a = -b\\)<br>\\((a + b)(b + c)(c + a) = (-c)(-a)(-b) = -abc\\)<br>\\(= -24\\), i.e. \\(\\boxed{-24}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): −24.</b>","hi":"\\(a + b + c = 0\\) से: \\(a + b = -c\\), \\(b + c = -a\\), \\(c + a = -b\\)<br>\\((a + b)(b + c)(c + a) = (-c)(-a)(-b) = -abc\\)<br>\\(= -24\\), अर्थात् \\(\\boxed{-24}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): −24 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000071755","section":"MATH","topic":"Percentage","question":{"en":"A family initially allocates 28% of its income to food, 24% to housing, 12% to transport, 16% to other expenses and saves the rest. Its income then rises by 25%; food expense rises by 15%, housing expense by 12.5%, transport expense falls by 10% and the amount saved rises by 50%. If the entire new income is accounted for, by what percentage does the amount spent on other expenses rise? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक परिवार शुरू में अपनी आय का 28% भोजन पर, 24% आवास पर, 12% परिवहन पर, 16% अन्य खर्चों पर व्यय करता है और शेष बचाता है। फिर उसकी आय 25% बढ़ जाती है; भोजन व्यय 15% बढ़ता है, आवास व्यय 12.5% बढ़ता है, परिवहन व्यय 10% घटता है और बचत 50% बढ़ जाती है। यदि पूरी नई आय का हिसाब हो जाता है, तो अन्य खर्चों पर किया गया व्यय कितने प्रतिशत बढ़ता है? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"52.25% increase"},"2":{"en":"55% increase"},"3":{"en":"56.25% increase"},"4":{"en":"60% increase"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Take the initial income as 100. Then food = 28, housing = 24, transport = 12, other = 16 and savings = 100 − (28 + 24 + 12 + 16) = 20<br>New income = 125<br>New food = \\(28 \\times 1.15 = 32.2\\); new housing = \\(24 \\times 1.125 = 27\\); new transport = \\(12 \\times 0.9 = 10.8\\); new savings = \\(20 \\times 1.5 = 30\\)<br>New other = \\(125 - (32.2 + 27 + 10.8 + 30) = 25\\)<br>Increase = \\(\\frac{25 - 16}{16} \\times 100 = \\frac{9}{16} \\times 100 = \\boxed{56.25\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 56.25% increase.</b>","hi":"प्रारंभिक आय 100 मानिए। तब भोजन = 28, आवास = 24, परिवहन = 12, अन्य = 16 और बचत = 100 − (28 + 24 + 12 + 16) = 20<br>नई आय = 125<br>नया भोजन = \\(28 \\times 1.15 = 32.2\\); नया आवास = \\(24 \\times 1.125 = 27\\); नया परिवहन = \\(12 \\times 0.9 = 10.8\\); नई बचत = \\(20 \\times 1.5 = 30\\)<br>नया अन्य = \\(125 - (32.2 + 27 + 10.8 + 30) = 25\\)<br>वृद्धि = \\(\\frac{25 - 16}{16} \\times 100 = \\frac{9}{16} \\times 100 = \\boxed{56.25\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 56.25% increase है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000071756","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Choose the correct indirect speech of the given sentence from the options below.<br>The teacher said to the student, “Finish your homework before class.” [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The teacher said the student must finish his homework before class."},"2":{"en":"The teacher told the student to finish his homework before class."},"3":{"en":"The teacher asked the student to finish his homework before class."},"4":{"en":"The teacher said that finish your homework before class."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: An imperative becomes “told + object + to-infinitive.”</b><br>The direct command becomes “told the student to finish his homework.”<br>“Said to” changes to “told” before the object.<br>The modal and “asked” versions alter the force or structure.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The teacher told the student to finish his homework before class.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000071757","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blanks with an appropriate degree of comparison.<br>Seldom have we encountered a theory ___ intriguing ___ this one. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"much, than"},"2":{"en":"more, than"},"3":{"en":"as, that"},"4":{"en":"more, as"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Comparative adjective + “than” compares two theories.</b><br>“More intriguing than this one” is the correct construction.<br>“Much … than” and “more … as” are ungrammatical.<br>“As … that” does not form the required comparison.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): more, than.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000071758","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br>While Gödel's incompleteness theorems,<br>P. demonstrating that in any sufficiently powerful formal system<br>Q. unprovable statements must necessarily exist<br>R. shattered the foundational ambitions of mathematical logic,<br>S. they also paradoxically reinforced its internal consistency [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PRSQ"},"2":{"en":"RQPS"},"3":{"en":"RSPQ"},"4":{"en":"PQRS"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RSPQ</b><br>R completes the first main clause: the theorems shattered foundational ambitions.<br>S adds the paradoxical reinforcement of consistency.<br>P and Q supply the demonstration that unprovable statements exist in powerful systems.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): RSPQ.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000071759","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br>The record-breaking performance<br>P. established a new world record<br>Q. after years of rigorous training<br>R. and was hailed as a historic achievement<br>S. by the young athlete at the championship [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"SPQR"},"2":{"en":"RSQP"},"3":{"en":"SRPQ"},"4":{"en":"PQSR"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: SPQR</b><br>S identifies the young athlete and the championship setting.<br>P gives the performance’s result: a world record.<br>Q supplies the preparation, and R concludes with its reception.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): SPQR.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000071760","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"What does the idiom “take the bull by the horns” mean? [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To face a difficult situation with courage and determination"},"2":{"en":"To avoid a problem by ignoring it"},"3":{"en":"To make a situation worse by interfering"},"4":{"en":"To give up easily when facing a challenge"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Take the bull by the horns (हिम्मत से सामना करना) = confront difficulty decisively.</b><br>Example: “She took the bull by the horns and addressed the funding crisis.”<br>Avoidance and surrender are opposite responses.<br>The idiom does not imply making matters worse.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): To face a difficult situation with courage and determination.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000071761","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the option that best improves the sentence by using the correct collocation highlighted in bold.<br>He <b>did an effort</b> to improve his writing skills. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"performed an effort"},"2":{"en":"made an effort"},"3":{"en":"took an effort"},"4":{"en":"created an effort"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Collocation: “Make an effort” means try hard.</b><br>Correct sentence: “He <b>made an effort</b> to improve his writing skills.”<br>“Perform,” “take” and “create” do not form the standard collocation with “an effort.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): made an effort.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000071762","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the option that best improves the sentence by using the correct collocation highlighted in bold.<br>The scientist <b>created a solution</b> to the complicated theory. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"came up with a solution"},"2":{"en":"created a resolution"},"3":{"en":"brought a solving"},"4":{"en":"took a solution"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Collocation: “Come up with a solution” means devise an answer.</b><br>The scientist devised a solution to the complicated theory.<br>“Resolution” concerns resolving a dispute or formal decision.<br>The other options are unidiomatic.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): came up with a solution.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000071763","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the appropriate tense.<br>If the team ___ the interim results more meticulously, the final report would not have contained so many discrepancies. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"analyze"},"2":{"en":"have analyzed"},"3":{"en":"had analyzed"},"4":{"en":"has analyzed"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Third conditional uses “if + past perfect” and “would have + past participle.”</b><br>“Had analyzed” expresses the unreal past condition.<br>The result “would not have contained” confirms the counterfactual structure.<br>The other forms do not fit.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): had analyzed.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000071764","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the appropriate tense.<br>Although the panel ___ several contentious issues during the discussion, it failed to reach a unanimous conclusion. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"addresses"},"2":{"en":"had addressed"},"3":{"en":"addressed"},"4":{"en":"was addressing"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Simple past describes the completed discussion.</b><br>“Addressed” parallels “failed” in the main clause.<br>Simple present and past perfect create unsuitable time relations.<br>Past continuous would emphasize an unfinished background action.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): addressed.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000071765","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom:<br>Brought into play [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Put under physical strain"},"2":{"en":"Engaged in recreational activity"},"3":{"en":"Made operational or effective"},"4":{"en":"Delayed unnecessarily"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Bring into play (लागू करना) = make something active or influential.</b><br>Example: “New safety measures were brought into play.”<br>The idiom does not refer specifically to physical strain or recreation.<br>It also does not mean delay.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Made operational or effective.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000071766","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom:<br>To pour new wine into old bottles [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To repeat history unnecessarily"},"2":{"en":"To disguise change as tradition"},"3":{"en":"To force a new idea into an outdated framework"},"4":{"en":"To dilute meaning through overuse"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Pour new wine into old bottles = place new ideas into unsuitable old structures.</b><br>Example: “The reforms merely poured new wine into old bottles.”<br>It concerns incompatibility between innovation and outdated frameworks.<br>Repetition, disguise and dilution are not the core meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): To force a new idea into an outdated framework.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000071767","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the correct spelling of a philosophical term. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Consciousness"},"2":{"en":"Conscienceness"},"3":{"en":"Conshousness"},"4":{"en":"Consciencenes"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Consciousness (चेतना) = awareness of oneself and the world.</b><br>The correct spelling is “consciousness.”<br><b>Conscienceness</b> substitutes “conscience” for “conscious.”<br><b>Conshousness</b> omits letters, and <b>consciencenes</b> is malformed.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Consciousness.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000071768","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the correct spelling of a blood-disorder term. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Thrombocytopaenia"},"2":{"en":"Thrombocytopenia"},"3":{"en":"Thrombocitopenia"},"4":{"en":"Thrombosytopenia"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Thrombocytopenia (प्लेटलेट्स की कमी) = an abnormally low platelet count.</b><br>The keyed spelling is “thrombocytopenia.”<br><b>Thrombocitopenia</b> uses “i” instead of “y.”<br><b>Thrombosytopenia</b> incorrectly uses “s.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Thrombocytopenia.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000071769","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Identify the misspelt word. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Obfuscate"},"2":{"en":"Dispondent"},"3":{"en":"Inveigle"},"4":{"en":"Capitulation"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Despondent (हतोत्साह) = dejected and hopeless.</b><br><b>Dispondent</b> incorrectly uses “i” instead of “e.”<br><b>Obfuscate</b> = make unclear; <b>inveigle</b> = persuade by flattery.<br><b>Capitulation</b> = surrender; these are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Dispondent.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000071770","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Identify the misspelt word. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Recondite"},"2":{"en":"Apothegm"},"3":{"en":"Impregnable"},"4":{"en":"Sagacius"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Sagacious (विवेकपूर्ण) = wise and discerning.</b><br><b>Sagacius</b> omits “o” before “u.”<br><b>Recondite</b> = obscure or abstruse.<br><b>Apothegm</b> = concise saying; <b>impregnable</b> = unconquerable.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Sagacius.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000071771","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:<br>Not only the students (1)/ but also the faculty members (2)/ was concerned about (3)/ the accreditation results. (4) [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: With “not only … but also,” the verb agrees with the nearer subject.</b><br>The nearer subject “faculty members” is plural.<br>Part (3) should read “<b>were concerned</b> about.”<br>The other parts are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): (3).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000071772","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:<br>The professor was appreciative (1)/ with the student's effort (2)/ in curating the bibliography (3)/ in multiple citation styles. (4) [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Appreciative of” is the standard construction.</b><br>Part (2) should read “<b>of the student’s effort</b>.”<br>“Appreciative with” is unidiomatic.<br>The remaining parts are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): (2).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000071773","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Select the sentence containing the homonym of the highlighted word:<br>He picked up a <b>rock</b> and threw it into the lake. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The kids climbed a big rock near the beach."},"2":{"en":"The band played rock music all night."},"3":{"en":"Their cottage stood beside a rock face."},"4":{"en":"She collected shiny rocks by the river."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rock = stone, or a genre of popular music.</b><br>The original uses the geological meaning.<br>Option B uses “rock” for music.<br>The other options retain the stone meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The band played rock music all night.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000071774","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Select the sentence containing the homonym of the highlighted word:<br>The scribe recorded a <b>bulla</b> at the bottom of the charter. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The medieval bulla sealed the papal decree."},"2":{"en":"The physician diagnosed the lesion as a bulla."},"3":{"en":"The diplomat delivered a golden bulla to the emperor."},"4":{"en":"The monk copied the Latin text below the bulla."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Bulla = an official seal, or a fluid-filled blister.</b><br>The original uses the documentary or seal meaning.<br>Option B uses the medical meaning of a large blister.<br>The other options retain the historical meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The physician diagnosed the lesion as a bulla.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000071775","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech.<br>The author said that so compelling was the plot that readers couldn’t put the book down. [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"“So compelling was the plot that readers couldn’t put the book down,” said the author."},"2":{"en":"“The plot was compelling, so readers kept reading,” said the author."},"3":{"en":"“It was such a compelling plot, readers read it all,” said the author."},"4":{"en":"“The plot made readers unable to stop,” said the author."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Preserve the emphatic inversion and idiomatic consequence.</b><br>A retains “So compelling was the plot that …” exactly.<br>It also retains “couldn’t put the book down.”<br>The other options paraphrase and lose parts of the original emphasis.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): “So compelling was the plot that readers couldn’t put the book down,” said the author.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000071776","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words from the options given below.<br><br>The concept of Smart Cities has emerged as a strategic response to the challenges of rapid urbanization. These cities integrate digital technologies with urban infrastructure to enhance efficiency, sustainability, and citizen welfare. (1)___, the deployment of sensors, data analytics, and artificial intelligence enables real-time monitoring of traffic, energy consumption, and waste management. The ultimate objective is not merely technological sophistication but the creation of inclusive and resilient urban ecosystems. (2)___, critics argue that excessive reliance on technology may marginalize communities lacking digital literacy or access.<br><br>The governance of Smart Cities requires a delicate balance between innovation and equity. Transparent data policies are essential; (3)___, concerns about privacy and surveillance remain unresolved. Moreover, the financial burden of establishing such infrastructure is considerable, and many developing nations face resource constraints. (4)___, international collaborations and public-private partnerships have become crucial in bridging these gaps.<br><br>Smart cities are often portrayed as futuristic utopias, yet their success depends on pragmatic implementation. They must prioritize human-centric design, ensuring that technology serves social needs rather than dictating them. (5)___, the vision of Smart Cities will remain aspirational unless grounded in participatory governance and sustainable planning.<br><br><br>Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank (1). [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Nevertheless"},"2":{"en":"For instance"},"3":{"en":"Conversely"},"4":{"en":"Meanwhile"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>For instance (उदाहरणतः) introduces a specific illustration.</b><br>Sensors and analytics exemplify the integration of technology with infrastructure.<br>“Nevertheless” and “conversely” signal contrast.<br>“Meanwhile” signals simultaneous action.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): For instance.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000071777","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words from the options given below.<br><br>The concept of Smart Cities has emerged as a strategic response to the challenges of rapid urbanization. These cities integrate digital technologies with urban infrastructure to enhance efficiency, sustainability, and citizen welfare. (1)___, the deployment of sensors, data analytics, and artificial intelligence enables real-time monitoring of traffic, energy consumption, and waste management. The ultimate objective is not merely technological sophistication but the creation of inclusive and resilient urban ecosystems. (2)___, critics argue that excessive reliance on technology may marginalize communities lacking digital literacy or access.<br><br>The governance of Smart Cities requires a delicate balance between innovation and equity. Transparent data policies are essential; (3)___, concerns about privacy and surveillance remain unresolved. Moreover, the financial burden of establishing such infrastructure is considerable, and many developing nations face resource constraints. (4)___, international collaborations and public-private partnerships have become crucial in bridging these gaps.<br><br>Smart cities are often portrayed as futuristic utopias, yet their success depends on pragmatic implementation. They must prioritize human-centric design, ensuring that technology serves social needs rather than dictating them. (5)___, the vision of Smart Cities will remain aspirational unless grounded in participatory governance and sustainable planning.<br><br><br>Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank (2). [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Therefore"},"2":{"en":"However"},"3":{"en":"Moreover"},"4":{"en":"Consequently"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>However (फिर भी) introduces a contrast.</b><br>Critics’ concerns about exclusion contrast with the benefits just described.<br>“Therefore” and “consequently” introduce results.<br>“Moreover” adds supporting information rather than opposition.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): However.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000071778","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words from the options given below.<br><br>The concept of Smart Cities has emerged as a strategic response to the challenges of rapid urbanization. These cities integrate digital technologies with urban infrastructure to enhance efficiency, sustainability, and citizen welfare. (1)___, the deployment of sensors, data analytics, and artificial intelligence enables real-time monitoring of traffic, energy consumption, and waste management. The ultimate objective is not merely technological sophistication but the creation of inclusive and resilient urban ecosystems. (2)___, critics argue that excessive reliance on technology may marginalize communities lacking digital literacy or access.<br><br>The governance of Smart Cities requires a delicate balance between innovation and equity. Transparent data policies are essential; (3)___, concerns about privacy and surveillance remain unresolved. Moreover, the financial burden of establishing such infrastructure is considerable, and many developing nations face resource constraints. (4)___, international collaborations and public-private partnerships have become crucial in bridging these gaps.<br><br>Smart cities are often portrayed as futuristic utopias, yet their success depends on pragmatic implementation. They must prioritize human-centric design, ensuring that technology serves social needs rather than dictating them. (5)___, the vision of Smart Cities will remain aspirational unless grounded in participatory governance and sustainable planning.<br><br><br>Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank (3). [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"since"},"2":{"en":"similarly"},"3":{"en":"indeed"},"4":{"en":"yet"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Yet (फिर भी) contrasts transparent policies with unresolved privacy concerns.</b><br>Transparent data policies are necessary, but surveillance worries persist.<br>“Since” would give a reason, and “similarly” a comparison.<br>“Indeed” would reinforce rather than contrast.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): yet.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000071779","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words from the options given below.<br><br>The concept of Smart Cities has emerged as a strategic response to the challenges of rapid urbanization. These cities integrate digital technologies with urban infrastructure to enhance efficiency, sustainability, and citizen welfare. (1)___, the deployment of sensors, data analytics, and artificial intelligence enables real-time monitoring of traffic, energy consumption, and waste management. The ultimate objective is not merely technological sophistication but the creation of inclusive and resilient urban ecosystems. (2)___, critics argue that excessive reliance on technology may marginalize communities lacking digital literacy or access.<br><br>The governance of Smart Cities requires a delicate balance between innovation and equity. Transparent data policies are essential; (3)___, concerns about privacy and surveillance remain unresolved. Moreover, the financial burden of establishing such infrastructure is considerable, and many developing nations face resource constraints. (4)___, international collaborations and public-private partnerships have become crucial in bridging these gaps.<br><br>Smart cities are often portrayed as futuristic utopias, yet their success depends on pragmatic implementation. They must prioritize human-centric design, ensuring that technology serves social needs rather than dictating them. (5)___, the vision of Smart Cities will remain aspirational unless grounded in participatory governance and sustainable planning.<br><br><br>Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank (4). [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Notwithstanding"},"2":{"en":"Otherwise"},"3":{"en":"Instead"},"4":{"en":"Nevertheless"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Nevertheless (इसके बावजूद) = despite the preceding difficulties.</b><br>Despite financial constraints, collaborations help bridge the gaps.<br>“Otherwise” introduces a consequence of non-action.<br>“Instead” introduces a substitute, and “notwithstanding” needs an object.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Nevertheless.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000071780","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words from the options given below.<br><br>The concept of Smart Cities has emerged as a strategic response to the challenges of rapid urbanization. These cities integrate digital technologies with urban infrastructure to enhance efficiency, sustainability, and citizen welfare. (1)___, the deployment of sensors, data analytics, and artificial intelligence enables real-time monitoring of traffic, energy consumption, and waste management. The ultimate objective is not merely technological sophistication but the creation of inclusive and resilient urban ecosystems. (2)___, critics argue that excessive reliance on technology may marginalize communities lacking digital literacy or access.<br><br>The governance of Smart Cities requires a delicate balance between innovation and equity. Transparent data policies are essential; (3)___, concerns about privacy and surveillance remain unresolved. Moreover, the financial burden of establishing such infrastructure is considerable, and many developing nations face resource constraints. (4)___, international collaborations and public-private partnerships have become crucial in bridging these gaps.<br><br>Smart cities are often portrayed as futuristic utopias, yet their success depends on pragmatic implementation. They must prioritize human-centric design, ensuring that technology serves social needs rather than dictating them. (5)___, the vision of Smart Cities will remain aspirational unless grounded in participatory governance and sustainable planning.<br><br><br>Select the most appropriate option to fill in blank (5). [SSC CGL 23/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"In contrast"},"2":{"en":"Without doubt"},"3":{"en":"After all"},"4":{"en":"Otherwise"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Otherwise (अन्यथा) introduces the result if the condition is not met.</b><br>Without participatory governance and sustainable planning, the vision remains aspirational.<br>“In contrast” introduces comparison, and “without doubt” expresses certainty.<br>“After all” gives a justification.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Otherwise.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};